    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A public health researcher is analyzing national survey data on the epidemiology of sexual violence in the United States. She wants to present accurate statistics regarding the lifetime prevalence of completed or attempted rape in women, as well as the proportion of these crimes that are actually reported to the police. Which of the following represents the correct statistical profile?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "5% lifetime risk; 90% are reported to the police",
      "B": "50% lifetime risk; 50% are reported to the police",
      "C": "10-15% lifetime risk; only 5% are reported to the police",
      "D": "Approximately 1 in 5 women (18-20% lifetime risk); only 10-15% are reported to the police",
      "E": "1 in 100 women lifetime risk; only 1% are reported to the police"
    },
    "correct": "D",
    "rationale": "are reported to the police \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Sexual Assault / Slide Rape / Passage 3 / 4 / 22 / 23 \u25cf Explanation: A. 5% lifetime risk; 90% are reported to the police: Incorrect. The lifetime risk is significantly higher, and the vast majority of cases are not reported to the police. B. 50% lifetime risk; 50% are reported to the police: Incorrect. This overestimates lifetime risk and significantly overestimates police reporting. C. 10-15% lifetime risk; only 5% are reported to the police: Incorrect. Approximately 18-20% of women report a lifetime history, and 10-15% of those are reported to the police. D. Approximately 1 in 5 women (18-20% lifetime risk); only 10-15% are reported to the police: Correct. According to ACOG and the National Violence Against Women Survey cited in the lecture, approximately 1 in 5 women (18% to 20%) in the U.S. experience completed or attempted rape over their lifetime. Additionally, sexual assault is highly underreported, with only 10% to 15% of cases reported to the police. E. 1 in 100 women lifetime risk; only 1% are reported to the police: Incorrect. This dramatically underestimates the prevalence of sexual assault.",
    "pearl": "",
    "learning_objectives": []
