    "rationale": "women \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Human Trafficking / Passage 7 / 26 \u25cf Explanation: A. Domestic violence; 90% are men: Incorrect. The presentation with a controlling manager and withheld documentation is highly specific for human trafficking, not isolated domestic violence. 100 B. Intimate partner conflict; equal distribution among genders: Incorrect. These symptoms are key \"red flags\" for human trafficking. C. Human trafficking (sexual or labor servitude); 71% of victims are women: Correct. Human trafficking is the illegal trade of human beings for use as commodities or objects in conditions of sexual or labor servitude. The lecture slides state that 71% of victims are women. The clinical signs described (controlling companion, submissive/fearful behavior, lack of documentation, untreated STIs) are classic \"Red Flags\" that a patient is a victim. D. Statutory exploitation; restricted entirely to minors under the age of 14: Incorrect. Human trafficking affects both adults and children; it is not restricted to minors under 14. E. Institutional neglect; occurring exclusively in correctional facilities: Incorrect. Human trafficking occurs in public and private spaces, not exclusively in prisons.",
