    "rationale": "101 \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Consequences Sexual Assault / Passage 8 / 27 \u25cf Explanation: A. 1% risk per rape; 10% risk if near ovulation: Incorrect. The average risk is 5%, and the risk near ovulation is 30%. B. 5% risk per rape; 30% risk if 1 to 2 days before ovulation: Correct. The lecture slides state that the risk of pregnancy per rape among females aged 12 to 45 years is 5%. However, if the rape occurs during the peak fertile window (1 to 2 days before ovulation), the risk of pregnancy increases to 30%. C. 10% risk per rape; 50% risk if near ovulation: Incorrect. These numbers are higher than those presented in the lecture. D. 20% risk per rape; 80% risk if 1 to 2 days before ovulation: Incorrect. These values are not supported by the lecture slides. E. 0.5% risk per rape; 5% risk if near ovulation: Incorrect. These values underestimate the real clinical risk of pregnancy following sexual assault.",
