    "rationale": "problems in adolescence and adulthood, as well as negative impacts on education and job opportunities \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Adverse Childhood Experiences / Passage 11 / 12 / 30 / 31 \u25cf Explanation: A. An increase in acute infectious diseases but no impact on chronic health conditions: Incorrect. ACEs are strongly linked to chronic health problems and mental illness, not just acute infectious diseases. B. Development of genetic chromosomal translocations and physical skeletal dysplasias: Incorrect. ACEs are environmental and psychological traumas; they do not cause primary genetic translocations or skeletal dysplasias. C. Chronic health problems, mental illness, and substance use problems in adolescence and adulthood, as well as negative impacts on education and job opportunities: Correct. The lecture slides state that Adverse Childhood Experiences (ACEs)\u2014such as abuse, neglect, witnessing domestic violence, or household dysfunction\u2014are directly linked to chronic health problems, mental illness, and substance use problems in adolescence and adulthood. Additionally, ACEs can negatively impact a person's education, job opportunities, and earning potential. D. A selective increase in gastrointestinal malignancies but no impact on socioeconomic parameters: Incorrect. The impacts of ACEs are widespread, affecting mental health, substance use, and multiple chronic diseases, as well as major socioeconomic parameters like job opportunities and earnings. E. Short-term behavioral issues that completely resolve by age 18 without long-term sequelae: Incorrect. The effects of ACEs are long-lasting and continue to affect individuals throughout their adult lives.",
