    "qnum": 96,
    "topic": "Sexual Assault and Abuse (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A gynecologist is performing a routine examination on an adult patient from an East African nation. The clinician notes that the patient's clitoral glans and clitoral hood are partially absent, but her labia minora and labia majora are completely intact and there is 95 no scarring over the vaginal opening. Which type of Female Genital Mutilation (FGM) does this represent?",
