    "topic": "Sexual Assault and Abuse (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 28-year-old female presents for preconception counseling. On physical examination, the clinician notes the complete absence of the clitoral glans, as well as the complete absence of the labia minora. The labia majora are partially scarred, but the vaginal opening is completely visible and unobstructed. How should this form of Female Genital Mutilation (FGM) be classified?",
