    "qnum": 98,
    "topic": "Sexual Assault and Abuse (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 22-year-old pregnant female presents for her first prenatal visit. On pelvic examination, the obstetrician is unable to insert a standard speculum because the vaginal opening is almost completely obstructed by a thick band of scar tissue formed by stitching the labia minora and majora over the vestibule. There is only a single, tiny opening at the inferior aspect to allow for the passage of urine. What is the classification and alternative name for this type of Female Genital Mutilation (FGM)?",
