    "rationale": "\u25cf Lecture Source: Slide 4 Major Types: Female Genital Mutilation / Passage 15 / 34 \u25cf Explanation: A. Type 1; Clitoridectomy: Incorrect. Type 1 involves only clitoral/prepuce tissue removal and does not obstruct the vaginal opening. B. Type 2; Excision: Incorrect. Type 2 involves excision of the clitoris and labia minora but does not close the vaginal introitus. C. Type 3; Infibulation: Correct. Type 3 FGM, also known as infibulation, involves the narrowing or obstruction of the vaginal opening by incising and stitching the labia minora and/or labia majora over the vestibule, with or without removal of the clitoris. This creates a covering seal, leaving only a tiny opening for the passage of urine and menstrual blood. D. Type 4; Introitus cauterization: Incorrect. Type 4 refers to procedures like pricking, piercing, scraping, or cauterizing that do not excise or suture the labia to close the introitus. 107 E. Type 1; Prepucectomization: Incorrect. This is a clinically incorrect term and does not represent Type 3 infibulation.",
