    "rationale": "\u25cf Lecture Source: Slide 4 Major Types: Female Genital Mutilation / Passage 15 / 34 \u25cf Explanation: A. It is not classified as FGM because no tissue was removed: Incorrect. The WHO explicitly classifies non-excisory traumatic procedures, including pricking, as FGM. B. Type 1 Female Genital Mutilation: Incorrect. Type 1 requires partial or total removal of the clitoral glans/prepuce. C. Type 2 Female Genital Mutilation: Incorrect. Type 2 requires removal of the clitoris and labia minora. D. Type 3 Female Genital Mutilation: Incorrect. Type 3 requires stitching of the labia to obstruct the vaginal opening. E. Type 4 Female Genital Mutilation: Correct. Type 4 FGM is defined as all other harmful/traumatic procedures to the female genitalia for non-medical purposes. This explicitly includes pricking, piercing, incising, scraping, and cauterizing the external genitalia, even if no tissue is permanently removed.",
