    "stem": "A 31-year-old G1P0 at 12 weeks gestation with a history of Type 1 Diabetes is seen for her routine prenatal visit. She is managed on a continuous subcutaneous insulin infusion pump. She is highly concerned that the insulin she infuses will cross the placenta and cause hypoglycemia or structural anomalies in her developing fetus. Which of the following biological principles best explains why maternal insulin does not easily cross the placental barrier?",
