    "stem": "A 27-year-old pregnant elementary school teacher presents to the clinic after being exposed to a student who was diagnosed with \"Fifth disease\" and presented with a classic \"slapped-cheek\" rash. Several weeks later, an obstetric ultrasound reveals significant fetal ascites, skin edema, and pleural effusion, consistent with hydrops fetalis. Which of the following options correctly identifies the causative pathogen and the primary mechanism behind these fetal findings?",
