    "rationale": "\u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Syphilis / Slide TORCH summary / Passage 5 / 10 / 27 / 29 / 42 \u25cf Explanation: A. Patent ductus arteriosus and cataracts: Incorrect. These are classic features of congenital Rubella. B. \"Blueberry muffin\" rash and periventricular calcifications: Incorrect. These are associated with congenital CMV. C. Rhinitis (\"snuffles\") and Hutchinson teeth: Correct. Congenital syphilis is caused by the transplacental transmission of the spirochete Treponema pallidum. Classic manifestations of congenital syphilis include persistent, highly infectious nasal discharge (\"snuffles\"), Hutchinson teeth (notched, peg-shaped incisors), saddle nose deformity, linear scars at the angles of the mouth (rhagades), and osteochondritis/saber shins. D. Phocomelia and limb reduction defects: Incorrect. Phocomelia is caused by thalidomide, not syphilis. 80 E. Aplasia cutis congenita and skeletal demineralization: Incorrect. Aplasia cutis congenita (localized absence of skin, typically on the scalp) is a classic side effect of methimazole exposure, not syphilis.",
