    "stem": "A 30-year-old G2P1 at 32 weeks gestation presents with sudden-onset, severe abdominal pain, uterine tenderness, and dark vaginal bleeding. An emergent ultrasound reveals a large retroplacental clot, confirming a placental abruption. Her toxicology screen is positive for cocaine. Which of the following represents the primary pathophysiology by which cocaine causes this acute obstetric complication? 71",
