    "rationale": "gestational age at exposure, with a classic teratogenic threshold dose of 0.05 Gray (50 mGy or 5 rad) \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Radiation / Slide Radiation Gestational Period Table / Slide Checkpoint Question #3 / Passage 1 / 13 / 14 / 32 / 33 / 43 \u25cf Explanation: A. Fetal injury risk is determined solely by maternal age, and there is no threshold dose for malformations: Incorrect. Maternal age is not a determinant of radiation-induced teratogenesis, and there is a clear, established threshold dose. B. The fetal risk is determined by both the fetal dose and the gestational age at exposure, with a classic teratogenic threshold dose of 0.05 Gray (50 mGy or 5 rad): Correct. The teratogenic risk of ionizing radiation is determined by two main factors: (1) the gestational age of the fetus at the time of exposure, and (2) the radiation dose absorbed by the fetus. According to the lecture materials, the established threshold dose for radiation-induced teratogenicity (structural malformations, microcephaly, intellectual disability) is 0.05 Gray (equivalent to 50 mGy or 5 rad). Standard diagnostic imaging (such as x-rays or CT scans, even of the pelvis) typically exposes the fetus to doses far below this threshold. C. Any diagnostic imaging study, including a single chest X-ray, exceeds the teratogenic threshold and causes phocomelia: Incorrect. A chest X-ray exposes the fetus to a negligible dose of <0.01 mGy, which is thousands of times below the 50 mGy threshold. Phocomelia is caused by thalidomide, not radiation. D. Radiation exposure is completely safe during organogenesis (weeks 2-8) but highly dangerous before implantation: Incorrect. Organogenesis is the most sensitive period for radiation-induced congenital anomalies (threshold 200 mGy). Before implantation, the risk is all-or-none (death or normal survival, threshold 50-100 mGy). 85 E. The threshold dose for severe intellectual disability is lowest during the late third trimester (weeks 36-40): Incorrect. The threshold for intellectual disability is lowest during the 8-15 week window of gestation (threshold 60-310 mGy) because this is the period of rapid neuronal development and migration.",
