    "stem": "A healthy 24-year-old female at 26 weeks gestation presents for a routine prenatal visit. She is feeling well but notes that her heart seems to \"beat a bit faster\" and she feels warmer than usual. Her vital signs are within normal limits for pregnancy, with a heart rate of 88 beats per minute (her pre-pregnancy heart rate was 72 beats per minute). The clinician explains that these are normal physiological adaptations. Which of the following best describes the timeline of the changes in stroke volume and cardiac output during a normal pregnancy?",
