    "stem": "A 25-year-old woman presents for routine preconception counseling. She has a history of generalized tonic-clonic epilepsy well-controlled on sodium valproate. Her past medical history is otherwise unremarkable. She takes no other medications. In addition to discussing antiepileptic drug optimization, the physician prescribes daily oral folic acid supplementation. Because of her anticonvulsant regimen, which of the following daily doses of folic acid should be recommended prior to conception and continued through the first trimester?",
