    "stem": "A 24-year-old Rh-negative primigravida at 28 weeks gestation presents for routine prenatal care. Her antibody screen (indirect Coombs test) is negative for anti-D antibodies. Her husband is known to be Rh-positive. The physician administers intramuscular Rho(D) immune globulin (RhoGAM). Which of the following best describes the molecular composition and mechanism of action of this medication in preventing Rh alloimmunization?",
