    "stem": "A 37-year-old primigravida at 11 weeks gestation undergoes first-trimester combined screening for fetal aneuploidy. Ultrasound examination demonstrates an increased fetal nuchal translucency of 3.8 mm (normal < 3.0 mm). Maternal serum biochemical testing demonstrates a pregnancy-associated plasma protein A (PAPP-A) level at 0.3 MoM (decreased) and a free beta-hCG level at 2.4 MoM (elevated). This pattern of first-trimester screening findings is most suggestive of which of the following fetal karyotypic abnormalities?",
