    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "- **Second-Trimester Quadruple Screen:** Performed between 15 and 20 weeks gestation to assess risks of Trisomy 21, Trisomy 18, and open neural tube defects.\n- **Trisomy 21 (Down Syndrome) Mnemonic:**\n  - **\"HI up is Down\"** -> **H**CG is **High** and **I**nhibin A is **High**.\n  - **MSAFP:** Decreased\n  - **Unconjugated estriol (uE3):** Decreased\n- **Comparison with Other Quad Screen Patterns:**\n  - **Trisomy 18 (Edwards Syndrome):** **All four markers are LOW or normal** (low AFP, low estriol, low hCG, low/normal inhibin A).\n  - **Open Neural Tube Defects (Anencephaly, Spina Bifida):** **MSAFP is markedly ELEVATED** (typically > 2.5 MoM) due to leakage of fetal protein through the unclosed defect into amniotic fluid and maternal circulation. Normal hCG, estriol, and inhibin A. Confirmed by elevated amniotic fluid AFP and **acetylcholinesterase (AChE)**.\n  - **Abdominal Wall Defects (Gastroschisis, Omphalocele):** Marked elevation of **MSAFP** with normal other markers.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Open neural tube defect & (D) Gastroschisis:** Characterized by isolated, marked elevation of MSAFP.\n  - **(B) Edwards syndrome:** Characterized by low hCG, low estriol, and low MSAFP (\"everything is low\").\n  - **(E) Fetal demise:** Causes precipitous collapse of placental steroidogenesis and fetal synthesis, showing low estriol and hCG.",
    "pearl": "**Quad Screen Summary:**\n- **Down syndrome (Trisomy 21):** High **H**CG, High **I**nhibin A, Low AFP, Low Estriol (**HI** is **Down**).\n- **Edwards syndrome (Trisomy 18):** Low HCG, Low Estriol, Low AFP, Normal/Low Inhibin (Everything Low).\n- **Neural tube defects / Gastroschisis / Omphalocele:** Isolated elevated **MSAFP** (confirm with amniotic **acetylcholinesterase** for NTD).",
