    "stem": "A 35-year-old female presents to the obstetrics clinic for her first prenatal visit. During the intake history, she reports the following obstetrical history: she has been pregnant a total of 8 times. She has had 4 full-term vaginal deliveries, 1 preterm delivery at 34 weeks gestation, 3 spontaneous abortions before 20 weeks gestation, and has 4 living children. Which of the following represents the correct gravidity and parity (FPAL) notation for this patient?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "G8 P4-1-4-3",
      "B": "G5 P4-1-3-4",
      "C": "G8 P4-3-1-4",
      "D": "G5 P4-3-1-4",
      "E": "G8 P4-1-3-4"
    },
    "correct": "E",
    "rationale": "\u25cf Lecture Source: Slide OB history / Passage 308 / Slide 22 \u25cf Explanation: A. G8 P4-1-4-3: Incorrect. This incorrectly lists 4 abortions and 3 living children. B. G5 P4-1-3-4: Incorrect. The gravidity must include all pregnancies, including abortions. Thus, gravidity is 8, not 5. C. G8 P4-3-1-4: Incorrect. This reverses the preterm and abortion categories. D. G5 P4-3-1-4: Incorrect. This has incorrect gravidity and switches preterm/abortions. E. G8 P4-1-3-4: Correct. Gravidity (G) represents the total number of pregnancies, regardless of outcome. Here, G = 8. Parity is recorded using the FPAL system: Full-term (F) deliveries (>= 37 weeks): 4; Preterm (P) deliveries (20 to 36 weeks): 1; Abortions (A) / losses (< 20 weeks): 3; Living children (L): 4. Thus, the patient's status is G8 P4-1-3-4.",
