    "correct": "D",
    "rationale": "\u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Dating the pregnancy / Passage 307 / 315 / Slide 26 \u25cf Explanation: A. July 8, 2026: Incorrect. This date is calculated by subtracting 7 days instead of adding them. B. July 15, 2026: Incorrect. This is exactly 9 months from the LMP, forgetting to add the 7 days of Naegele's rule. C. July 20, 2026: Incorrect. This is an incorrect calculation. D. July 22, 2026: Correct. Naegele's rule is used to estimate the Estimated Date of Confinement (EDC) or Delivery (EDD). The formula is: first day of LMP minus 3 months plus 7 days. Starting with October 15, 2025: subtracting 3 months gives July 15, and adding 7 days gives July 22, 2026. E. August 22, 2026: Incorrect. This is one month too late. 21",
