    "rationale": "vein \u2192 Circumflex vein \u2192 Deep dorsal vein \u2192 Periprostatic venous plexus \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Venous Drainage / Passage 3 \u25cf Explanation: A. Emissary vein \u2192 Sinusoidal venules \u2192 Subtunical venular plexus \u2192 Deep dorsal vein \u2192 Circumflex vein \u2192 Periprostatic venous plexus: Incorrect. This reverses the flow; sinusoids are the initial capillaries, and emissary veins lie downstream of subtunical plexus. B. Sinusoidal venules \u2192 Subtunical venular plexus \u2192 Emissary vein \u2192 Circumflex vein \u2192 Deep dorsal vein \u2192 Periprostatic venous plexus: Correct. The venous drainage of the corpora cavernosa follows a strict sequence: Sinusoidal Venules \u2192 Subtunical Venular Plexus \u2192 Emissary Vein \u2192 Circumflex Vein \u2192 Deep Dorsal Vein \u2192 Periprostatic Venous Plexus. 159 C. Circumflex vein \u2192 Sinusoidal venules \u2192 Subtunical venular plexus \u2192 Emissary vein \u2192 Periprostatic venous plexus \u2192 Deep dorsal vein: Incorrect. Circumflex veins drain emissary veins and feed into the deep dorsal vein. D. Deep dorsal vein \u2192 Emissary vein \u2192 Sinusoidal venules \u2192 Subtunical venular plexus \u2192 Circumflex vein \u2192 Periprostatic venous plexus: Incorrect. The deep dorsal vein is a large collecting vein near the exit of the pathway, not the start. E. Sinusoidal venules \u2192 Deep dorsal vein \u2192 Emissary vein \u2192 Subtunical venular plexus \u2192 Circumflex vein \u2192 Periprostatic venous plexus: Incorrect. This scrambles the relative microscopic-to-macroscopic order of venous channels.",
