    "correct": "E",
    "rationale": "adrenergic receptors, triggering the Phospholipase C/IP3 pathway to increase intracellular Calcium \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Penile Smooth Muscle Contraction / Passage 5 \u25cf Explanation: A. Parasympathetic release of Nitric Oxide; activates Guanylyl Cyclase to increase cGMP: Incorrect. This pathway drives smooth muscle relaxation and erection. B. Sympathetic release of Norepinephrine; activates Adenylate Cyclase to increase cAMP: Incorrect. cAMP reduces calcium and promotes relaxation; sympathetics inhibit cAMP. C. Parasympathetic release of Acetylcholine; inhibits Phospholipase C to decrease intracellular Calcium: Incorrect. Parasympathetic acetylcholine indirectly facilitates erection, not detumescence. D. Sympathetic release of Epinephrine; activates beta-2 adrenergic receptors to decrease intracellular Calcium: Incorrect. Beta-2 activation relaxes smooth muscle, whereas contraction is driven by alpha-1 adrenergic receptors. E. Sympathetic release of Norepinephrine; activates alpha-1 adrenergic receptors, triggering the Phospholipase C/IP3 pathway to increase intracellular Calcium: Correct. Detumescence is a sympathetic-mediated process. Sympathetic fibers release norepinephrine (NE) which binds to alpha-1 adrenergic receptors. This activates the Phospholipase C / IP3 pathway, increasing intracellular calcium, causing smooth muscle contraction and closing the helicine arterioles to drain the sinusoids.",
