    "rationale": "spermatocyte \u2192 Spermatid \u2192 Spermatozoan; Primary spermatocyte undergoes Meiosis I \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Learning Objectives / Slide Spermatogenesis / Slide Seminiferous Tubules / Passage 2 / 4 \u25cf Explanation: 140 A. Spermatogonium \u2192 Secondary spermatocyte \u2192 Primary spermatocyte \u2192 Spermatid \u2192 Spermatozoan; Secondary spermatocyte undergoes Meiosis I: Incorrect. Primary spermatocytes precede secondary spermatocytes and undergo the first meiotic division. B. Spermatogonium \u2192 Primary spermatocyte \u2192 Secondary spermatocyte \u2192 Spermatid \u2192 Spermatozoan; Primary spermatocyte undergoes Meiosis I: Correct. The correct sequence of germ cell progression is: Spermatogonium (diploid stem cell, 2n) \u2192 Primary spermatocyte (diploid, 2n, undergoes Meiosis I) \u2192 Secondary spermatocyte (haploid, 1n, undergoes Meiosis II) \u2192 Spermatid (haploid, 1n, undergoes spermiogenesis/differentiation) \u2192 Spermatozoan (mature sperm, 1n). C. Spermatid \u2192 Primary spermatocyte \u2192 Secondary spermatocyte \u2192 Spermatogonium \u2192 Spermatozoan; Spermatid undergoes Meiosis I: Incorrect. This reverses the developmental sequence; spermatogonium is the initial diploid stem cell, and spermatids are haploid products. D. Primary spermatocyte \u2192 Secondary spermatocyte \u2192 Spermatogonium \u2192 Spermatid \u2192 Spermatozoan; Spermatogonium undergoes Meiosis I: Incorrect. Spermatogonia undergo mitosis to self-renew and differentiate into primary spermatocytes, not meiosis. E. Spermatogonium \u2192 Spermatid \u2192 Primary spermatocyte \u2192 Secondary spermatocyte \u2192 Spermatozoan; Spermatozoan undergoes Meiosis I: Incorrect. Spermatids are formed after meiosis is complete, and mature spermatozoa do not undergo further division.",
