    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A urology resident is reviewing the anatomical pathway of sperm transport and maturation. She traces the movement of sperm from their site of production in the seminiferous tubules to their site of ejaculation. Which of the following pathways represents the correct sequence of structures, and where do sperm acquire forward motility and fertilization capacity?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Epididymis \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Efferent ductules \u2192 Vas deferens; mature and acquire motility in the vas deferens",
      "B": "Epididymis \u2192 Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Efferent ductules \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Vas deferens; mature and acquire motility in the seminiferous tubules",
      "C": "Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Vas deferens \u2192 Epididymis \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Efferent ductules; mature and acquire motility in the efferent ductules",
      "D": "Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Efferent ductules \u2192 Epididymis \u2192 Vas deferens; mature and acquire motility in the caput to cauda of the epididymis",
      "E": "Vas deferens \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Efferent ductules \u2192 Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Epididymis; mature and acquire motility in the seminal vesicles"
    },
    "correct": "D",
    "rationale": "Epididymis \u2192 Vas deferens; mature and acquire motility in the caput to cauda of the epididymis \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Sperm Transport / Passage 5 \u25cf Explanation: A. Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Epididymis \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Efferent ductules \u2192 Vas deferens; mature and acquire motility in the vas deferens: Incorrect. Epididymis is located after the efferent ductules, not before the rete testes. B. Epididymis \u2192 Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Efferent ductules \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Vas deferens; mature and acquire motility in the seminiferous tubules: Incorrect. Sperm are produced in the seminiferous tubules, not the epididymis, and are immotile when they leave the tubules. C. Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Vas deferens \u2192 Epididymis \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Efferent ductules; mature and acquire motility in the efferent ductules: Incorrect. This scrambles the physical pathway; the epididymis and efferent ductules precede the vas deferens. D. Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Efferent ductules \u2192 Epididymis \u2192 Vas deferens; mature and acquire motility in the caput to cauda of the epididymis: Correct. Sperm are produced in the seminiferous tubules and travel through the network of the rete testes into the efferent ductules. The efferent ductules empty into the epididymis. During their transport from the caput (head) to the cauda (tail) of the epididymis, sperm undergo structural and functional maturation, acquiring progressive forward motility and fertilization capacity. They are stored in the cauda of the epididymis until ejaculation, when they travel through the vas deferens. E. Vas deferens \u2192 Rete testes \u2192 Efferent ductules \u2192 Seminiferous tubules \u2192 Epididymis; mature and acquire motility in the seminal vesicles: Incorrect. This pathway is completely reversed and anatomically impossible.",
