    "topic": "HPT Axis & Disorders of Male (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A tall, 28-year-old male presents with primary infertility and bilateral breast enlargement (gynecomastia). Physical exam reveals extremely small, firm testes (<2 mL volume) and a female-type pubic hair pattern. A semen analysis reveals azoospermia. 134 His hormone profile shows: low testosterone, markedly elevated LH, and markedly elevated FSH. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis, what is his expected karyotype, and what percentage of patients can have sperm retrieved for IVF/ICSI?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Klinefelter's Syndrome; 47,XXY; 50-75% sperm retrieval via Micro-TESE",
      "B": "Kallmann Syndrome; 46,XY; 0% sperm retrieval",
      "C": "Noonan Syndrome; 45,X; 10% sperm retrieval",
      "D": "Sertoli-only Syndrome; 46,XX; 100% sperm retrieval",
      "E": "Prader-Willi Syndrome; 47,XYY; 25% sperm retrieval"
    },
    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "Micro-TESE \u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Chromosomal Anomalies / Slide Hypergonadotropic Hypogonadism / Passage 10 / 11 / 12 \u25cf Explanation: A. Klinefelter's Syndrome; 47,XXY; 50-75% sperm retrieval via Micro-TESE: Correct. Klinefelter's Syndrome (47,XXY) is the most common karyotypic cause of male infertility (representing 66% of karyotype abnormalities in infertile men). It presents with primary testicular failure (hypergonadotropic hypogonadism: low testosterone, elevated LH and FSH), small, firm testes (due to seminiferous tubule dysgenesis and fibrosis), azoospermia, gynecomastia, tall stature, and a female pubic hair pattern. Despite azoospermia in the ejaculate, microdissection testicular sperm extraction (Micro-TESE) can successfully retrieve viable sperm from isolated pockets of spermatogenesis in 50-75% of patients. B. Kallmann Syndrome; 46,XY; 0% sperm retrieval: Incorrect. Kallmann's is 46,XY and features hypogonadotropic hypogonadism, not small, firm testes or markedly elevated FSH/LH. C. Noonan Syndrome; 45,X; 10% sperm retrieval: Incorrect. Noonan is 46,XY (Male Turner's phenotype) and features cryptorchidism and short stature. D. Sertoli-only Syndrome; 46,XX; 100% sperm retrieval: Incorrect. Sertoli-only is 46,XY and features normal testosterone/LH with selectively elevated FSH. Sperm retrieval rates are 25-50%. E. Prader-Willi Syndrome; 47,XYY; 25% sperm retrieval: Incorrect. Prader-Willi is associated with chromosome 15 deletions, not 47,XYY, and features hypogonadotropic hypogonadism.",
    "pearl": "",
