    "topic": "HPT Axis & Disorders of Male (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 16-year-old boy is evaluated by a pediatric urologist. On physical exam, he is noted to have short stature, a webbed neck, low-set ears, a history of pulmonary stenosis, and bilateral undescended testes (cryptorchidism). His karyotype is reported as 46,XY. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
