    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "\u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Hypergonadotropic Hypogonadism / Passage 11 \u25cf Explanation: A. Klinefelter's Syndrome: Incorrect. Klinefelter's features tall stature, gynecomastia, and a 47,XXY karyotype. B. Kallmann Syndrome: Incorrect. Kallmann's features normal stature, anosmia, and hypogonadotropic hypogonadism. C. Noonan Syndrome (\"Male Turner's\"): Correct. Noonan Syndrome (46,XY) is an autosomal dominant condition often referred to as \"Male Turner's\" because it shares physical characteristics with Turner syndrome (45,X), including short stature, webbed neck, low-set ears, 145 and lymphedema. It is classically associated with pulmonary valve stenosis and cryptorchidism (undescended testes), which leads to hypergonadotropic hypogonadism. D. Prader-Willi Syndrome: Incorrect. Prader-Willi features obesity, hypotonicity, and hypogonadotropic hypogonadism. E. Laurence-Moon-Biedl Syndrome: Incorrect. Laurence-Moon-Biedl features polydactyly, retinitis pigmentosa, and obesity.",
