    "rationale": "\u25cf Lecture Source: Slide Hypogonadotropic Hypogonadism / Passage 10 / 11 \u25cf Explanation: A. Prader-Willi Syndrome: Correct. Prader-Willi Syndrome is a genetic disorder (classically due to deletion of the paternal copy of genes on Chromosome 15) characterized by severe infantile hypotonicity, mental retardation, hyperphagia leading to early-onset morbid obesity, and small hands and feet. It causes hypogonadotropic hypogonadism (absent GnRH drive), presenting with delayed puberty, microphallus, and cryptorchidism. B. Klinefelter's Syndrome: Incorrect. Klinefelter's is a hypergonadotropic hypogonadal state and does not feature severe childhood hypotonicity or obesity. C. Noonan Syndrome: Incorrect. Noonan syndrome features short stature, webbed neck, and pulmonary stenosis, without severe obesity or hypotonicity. D. Sertoli-only Syndrome: Incorrect. Sertoli-only features normal childhood development, normal body weight, and normal testosterone/LH. E. 5-alpha-reductase deficiency: Incorrect. 5-alpha-reductase deficiency features ambiguous genitalia at birth, but normal childhood weight, muscle tone, and normal central GnRH drive.",
