    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "- **Congenital Syphilis Spectrum (*Treponema pallidum*):**\n  - **Early Congenital Syphilis (Manifestations before age 2, typically within the first 3 months):**\n    1. **Syphilitic Rhinitis (\"Snuffles\"):** Highly infectious, purulent, serosanguinous/bloody nasal discharge loaded with live spirochetes; appears within the first few weeks of life.\n    2. **Cutaneous Lesions:** Maculopapular, copper-red or dusky-red eruption with **profuse desquamation (peeling)** affecting the **palms and soles**; condylomata lata in moist anogenital folds.\n    3. **Skeletal Lesions:** Osteochondritis and periostitis (seen in $>70\\%$ of early cases). **Wimberger sign** (focal demineralization and serrated destruction of the medial upper tibial metaphysis); painful periostitis causes refusal to move the limb (\"pseudoparalysis of Parrot\").\n    4. Hepatosplenomegaly, Coombs-negative hemolytic anemia, thrombocytopenia, and generalized lymphadenopathy.\n  - **Late Congenital Syphilis (Manifestations after age 2; chronic persistent inflammation and scarring):**\n    1. **Hutchinson Triad:**\n       - **Notched, peg-shaped Hutchinson incisors** (hypoplasia of central incisors).\n       - **Interstitial keratitis** (clouding of the cornea leading to blindness).\n       - **Eighth cranial nerve sensorineural deafness**.\n    2. **Craniofacial Deformities:** **Saddle nose** (destruction of nasal septum), **frontal bossing** of the forehead, high-arched palate.\n    3. **Dental Anomalies:** **Mulberry molars** (multiple rounded cusps on first molars).\n    4. **Skeletal Deformities:** **Saber shins** (anterior outward bowing of the tibia), **Clutton joints** (painless, symmetric, bilateral knee effusions).\n    5. **Rhagades:** Linear, radiating scars and fissures around the corners of the mouth and nose.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B) Toxoplasmosis, (C) Rubella, (D) CMV, & (E) Varicella:** Distinct TORCH syndromes described in detail in previous rationales. None produce the classic skeletal periostitis, snuffles, or Hutchinson triad.",
    "pearl": "**Congenital Syphilis:**\n- **Early (<2 years):** **Snuffles** (bloody nasal discharge), **desquamating rash on palms/soles**, periostitis / **Wimberger sign**.\n- **Late (>2 years):** **Hutchinson Triad** (notched incisors, interstitial keratitis, 8th nerve deafness), **Mulberry molars**, **Saddle nose**, **Saber shins**, and **Clutton joints**.",
