    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "- **Isotretinoin (Accutane / 13-cis-retinoic acid) Teratogenesis:**\n  - Synthetic derivative of Vitamin A (retinoid).\n  - Teratogenic risk exceeds **20\u201335%**, with an additional ~40% rate of spontaneous abortion.\n  - **Mechanism:** Retinoic acid is a critical morphogen that binds retinoic acid receptors (RAR/RXR) to regulate Hox gene expression and govern the migration and survival of **cranial neural crest cells**. Exogenous high-dose isotretinoin disrupts branchial arch and pharyngeal pouch morphogenesis.\n  - **Classic Phenotype (Retinoic Acid Embryopathy):**\n    1. **Craniofacial Anomalies:** Severe **microtia (rudimentary external ears) or anotia (complete absence of ears)**, stenotic external auditory canals, micrognathia, flat midface, and cleft palate.\n    2. **Central Nervous System Malformations:** Hydrocephalus, microcephaly, cerebellar hypoplasia, and cognitive impairment.\n    3. **Cardiovascular / Conotruncal Defects:** Transposition of the great arteries, tetralogy of Fallot, persistent truncus arteriosus, and interrupted aortic arch (similar to DiGeorge syndrome).\n    4. **Thymic and Parathyroid Abnormalities:** Absent or hypoplastic thymus (impaired T-cell immunity) and hypoparathyroidism.\n- **iPLEDGE Program Requirements:**\n  - Females of childbearing potential must have **two negative pregnancy tests** prior to initiating therapy.\n  - Must commit to using **two effective forms of contraception** concurrently starting 1 month before therapy, during therapy, and continuing for at least 1 month after discontinuing isotretinoin.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B) Phocomelia:** Classic teratogenic manifestation of **Thalidomide**.\n  - **(C) Ebstein anomaly:** Classic teratogenic anomaly of **Lithium**.\n  - **(D) Clear cell adenocarcinoma:** Caused by in utero exposure to **Diethylstilbestrol (DES)**.\n  - **(E) Chondrodysplasia punctata:** Hallmark of **Warfarin embryopathy**.",
    "pearl": "**Isotretinoin (Retinoid) Embryopathy:** Disrupts **cranial neural crest migration**.\n- **Ears:** **Microtia / anotia** (absent or tiny ears).\n- **Heart:** **Conotruncal cardiac defects** (truncus arteriosus, tetralogy of Fallot).\n- **Thymus:** **Thymic aplasia** (DiGeorge-like phenotype).\n- **Strict iPLEDGE:** 2 negative pregnancy tests $+$ 2 forms of contraception.",
