    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "- **Lithium Teratogenicity & Ebstein Anomaly:**\n  - Lithium carbonate is a gold-standard mood stabilizer for Bipolar Disorder, but first-trimester exposure carries an increased risk of congenital cardiovascular malformations, most classically **Ebstein anomaly**.\n  - **Anatomy & Pathophysiology of Ebstein Anomaly:**\n    1. **Apical Displacement:** The septal and posterior leaflets of the **tricuspid valve are abnormally displaced downward (apically)** toward the cardiac apex into the right ventricle, rather than attaching to the fibrous annulus.\n    2. **\"Atrialization\" of the Right Ventricle:** The upper portion of the right ventricle is incorporated into the right atrium, creating a **massively enlarged right atrium** and a small, hypoplastic, functionally compromised remaining right ventricle.\n    3. **Tricuspid Regurgitation:** Malformed leaflets fail to coapt, resulting in severe tricuspid regurgitation, right-sided heart failure, and cardiomegaly (classic \"box-shaped\" or spherical heart on chest radiography).\n    4. **Conduction Abnormalities:** Strongly associated with an accessory atrioventricular conduction pathway (**Wolff-Parkinson-White [WPW] syndrome**) causing paroxysmal supraventricular tachycardia, as well as right bundle branch block.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Tetralogy of Fallot:** VSD, overriding aorta, pulmonic stenosis, RVH; linked to maternal diabetes, retinoic acid, and 22q11.2 deletion.\n  - **(B) Coarctation of the aorta:** Narrowing of the aortic arch near the ductus arteriosus; classically linked to Turner syndrome (45,X).\n  - **(D) Transposition of the great arteries:** Aorta arises from RV and pulmonary trunk from LV; #1 cardiac anomaly in maternal pregestational diabetes.\n  - **(E) Tricuspid atresia:** Complete absence of the tricuspid orifice with hypoplastic RV; distinct from Ebstein displacement.",
    "pearl": "**Lithium in Pregnancy:** Associated with **Ebstein Anomaly**:\n- **Apical displacement of tricuspid valve leaflets**.\n- **\"Atrialization\" of the right ventricle** (huge RA, tiny functional RV).\n- Severe tricuspid regurgitation.\n- Associated with **Wolff-Parkinson-White (WPW) syndrome**!",
