    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "- **Maternal Tobacco Smoking in Pregnancy:**\n  - Cigarette smoking is the **#1 leading preventable cause of low birth weight and intrauterine growth restriction (IUGR)** in developed nations.\n  - **Two Primary Pathophysiologic Mechanisms:**\n    1. **Nicotine:** A potent sympathomimetic that stimulates maternal catecholamine release, producing severe **vasoconstriction of uterine and placental spiral arteries**, markedly reducing uteroplacental blood flow and fetal nutrient delivery.\n    2. **Carbon Monoxide (CO):** Readily crosses the placenta and binds fetal hemoglobin with an affinity $>200$ times higher than oxygen, forming **carboxyhemoglobin**. This competitively blocks oxygen binding and shifts the fetal oxygen-hemoglobin dissociation curve to the left (the Haldane effect), causing severe **fetal tissue hypoxia**.\n  - **Associated Obstetric & Neonatal Complications:**\n    - **Placental Complications:** **Placental abruption (abruptio placentae)** (due to decidual necrosis and spiral artery rupture) and **placenta previa**.\n    - **Pregnancy Loss:** Spontaneous abortion and stillbirth.\n    - **Preterm Delivery:** Preterm premature rupture of membranes (PPROM) and preterm labor.\n    - **Postnatal Morbidity:** **Sudden Infant Death Syndrome (SIDS)** (smoking is the leading maternal risk factor), childhood asthma, otitis media, and ADHD.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B), (C), (D), & (E):** While smoke contains hundreds of toxic compounds (cyanide, cadmium, hydrocarbons), tissue hypoxia from nicotine-induced vasoconstriction and carbon monoxide is the primary, proven driver of growth restriction.",
    "pearl": "**Cigarette Smoking in Pregnancy:** **#1 cause of preventable low birth weight / IUGR**.\n- **Nicotine:** Potent **vasoconstriction** $\\rightarrow$ $\\downarrow$ placental blood flow.\n- **Carbon Monoxide:** Forms **carboxyhemoglobin** $\\rightarrow$ fetal tissue hypoxia.\n- Greatly increases risk of **Placental Abruption**, **Placenta Previa**, **Preterm Labor**, and **SIDS**.",
