    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "- **Maternal Cocaine Abuse & Placental Abruption:**\n  - The patient has classic signs of **placental abruption (abruptio placentae)**: sudden-onset severe abdominal pain, uterine hypertonicity/rigidity (\"board-like\" uterus), dark vaginal bleeding, and non-reassuring fetal status/bradycardia.\n  - **Toxicology Screen:** Benzoylecgonine is the primary, long-lasting urinary metabolite of **cocaine**.\n  - **Mechanism of Cocaine:**\n    - Cocaine competitively **blocks the presynaptic monoamine reuptake transporters** for **norepinephrine (NET)**, dopamine (DAT), and serotonin (SERT).\n    - This results in massive accumulation of norepinephrine in the synaptic cleft of the sympathetic nervous system, inducing intense, profound **vasospasm of the decidual and spiral arterioles** combined with acute maternal hypertension.\n  - **Pathogenesis of Abruption:**\n    - Intense vasospasm of spiral arteries causes acute decidual ischemia and necrosis.\n    - Subsequent abrupt reperfusion or hypertensive shear stress ruptures the fragile decidual vessels, creating a **retroplacental hematoma** that dissects along the decidua basalis, shearing the placenta completely off the myometrial wall.\n  - **Other Complications of Prenatal Cocaine:**\n    - Severe intrauterine growth restriction (IUGR), low birth weight, microcephaly.\n    - Preterm delivery and premature rupture of membranes.\n    - Fetal vascular disruptions (e.g., intestinal atresia, limb amputations).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Placenta previa:** Characterized by **PAINLESS, bright red vaginal bleeding** without uterine tenderness or hypertonicity.\n  - **(C) Uterine rupture:** Presents with sudden loss of fetal station, palpable fetal parts in the abdomen, and cessation of contractions, typically in patients with prior uterine scars.\n  - **(D) Vasa previa:** Painless bleeding occurring immediately upon rupture of membranes with rapid fetal exsanguination.\n  - **(E) Chorioamnionitis:** Intrauterine infection presenting with fever, uterine tenderness, and foul-smelling lochia.",
    "pearl": "**Cocaine in Pregnancy:**\n- Blocks **presynaptic norepinephrine reuptake** $\\rightarrow$ massive vasoconstriction and hypertension.\n- Leading cause of **PLACENTAL ABRUPTION (Abruptio Placentae)**: **Painful**, dark red bleeding with a **rigid, hypertonic \"board-like\" uterus** and fetal distress.\n- Causes **IUGR**, preterm delivery, and fetal vascular disruptive anomalies.",
