    "rationale": "- **Antithyroid Medications & Teratogenicity:**\n  - Treatment of hyperthyroidism (Graves disease) in pregnancy requires careful drug selection based on gestational trimester.\n  - **Methimazole (and its prodrug Carbimazole):**\n    - Thionamide that inhibits thyroid peroxidase (TPO), blocking iodination of tyrosine and coupling of iodotyrosines.\n    - **Teratogenic Effects (Methimazole Embryopathy):** First-trimester exposure is associated with:\n      1. **Aplasia Cutis Congenita:** Congenital absence of skin, classically presenting as a solitary, well-demarcated, punched-out, non-scarred ulceration on the **midline scalp vertex**.\n      2. **Choanal Atresia:** Congenital membranous or bony obstruction of the posterior nasal apertures.\n      3. **Esophageal Atresia / Tracheoesophageal Fistula**.\n      4. Facial dysmorphism.\n- **Management Strategy for Hyperthyroidism in Pregnancy (Board Rule):**\n  - **First Trimester:** Use **Propylthiouracil (PTU)**! PTU carries a lower risk of major teratogenic malformations during the critical period of organogenesis (weeks 3\u20138).\n  - **Second and Third Trimesters:** Switch from PTU to **Methimazole**! PTU carries a black-box warning for **severe, fulminant maternal hepatotoxicity** (drug-induced acute liver failure requiring liver transplantation). Because organogenesis is complete by week 10, switching to methimazole avoids PTU-induced liver failure while posing minimal teratogenic risk to the fetus.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Propylthiouracil (PTU):** Does not cause aplasia cutis congenita; drug of choice in the 1st trimester (switched in 2nd trimester due to maternal hepatotoxicity).\n  - **(C) Potassium iodide:** High-dose iodine causes fetal goiter and congenital hypothyroidism (Wolff-Chaikoff effect).\n  - **(D) Propranolol:** Used for symptomatic tachycardia; chronic use can cause fetal growth restriction, but not aplasia cutis.\n  - **(E) Levothyroxine:** Treatment for hypothyroidism, does not cause birth defects.",
    "pearl": "**Hyperthyroidism in Pregnancy (High-Yield Switch):**\n- **1st Trimester:** **Propylthiouracil (PTU)** (prevents **Methimazole-induced Aplasia Cutis Congenita** [scalp defect] and choanal atresia).\n- **2nd & 3rd Trimesters:** **Switch to Methimazole** (prevents **PTU-induced fulminant hepatic necrosis** in the mother!).",
