    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "- **Antimicrobial Teratogenicity & Fetal Toxicities in Pregnancy:**\n  1. **Aminoglycosides (Gentamicin, Tobramycin, Streptomycin, Amikacin):**\n     - Freely cross the placenta and concentrate in fetal endolymph, perilymph, and renal proximal tubular cells.\n     - Selectively destroy sensory hair cells in the cochlea and vestibular apparatus, causing **irreversible bilateral sensorineural deafness (ototoxicity)** and **nephrotoxicity** (CN VIII damage).\n  2. **Tetracyclines (Doxycycline, Tetracycline, Minocycline):**\n     - Chelate divalent calcium cations and incorporate into fetal bones and deciduous teeth.\n     - Causes **permanent yellow-to-brown discoloration of primary dentition**, dental enamel hypoplasia, and transient suppression of long bone growth.\n  3. **Fluoroquinolones (Ciprofloxacin, Levofloxacin):**\n     - High affinity for developing connective tissue and articular cartilage; causes **cartilage toxicity, chondrodysplasia, and permanent arthropathy** in weight-bearing joints of juvenile animals.\n  4. **Sulfonamides (Sulfamethoxazole):**\n     - Administered near term, sulfonamides cross the placenta and **competitively displace unconjugated bilirubin from serum albumin**. Free lipid-soluble bilirubin crosses the immature fetal blood-brain barrier, depositing in the basal ganglia to cause **neonatal kernicterus** (bilirubin encephalopathy).\n  5. **Chloramphenicol:**\n     - Neonatal liver has immature glucuronyl transferase activity. Drug accumulation inhibits mitochondrial protein synthesis in the myocardium and vascular smooth muscle, causing **Gray Baby Syndrome** (cyanosis, ashen gray skin, cardiovascular collapse, and shock).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B) Tetracyclines:** Cause teeth discoloration and bone growth inhibition, not craniosynostosis.\n  - **(C) Fluoroquinolones:** Cause cartilage damage, not gray baby syndrome.\n  - **(D) Sulfonamides:** Cause kernicterus, not cartilage erosion.\n  - **(E) Chloramphenicol:** Causes gray baby syndrome, not tooth staining.",
    "pearl": "**Antimicrobial Fetal Toxicities (High-Yield Mnemonic):**\n- **Aminoglycosides:** **CN VIII Ototoxicity** (sensorineural deafness).\n- **Tetracyclines:** **Teeth discoloration** (yellow-brown) & bone growth delay.\n- **Fluoroquinolones:** **Cartilage damage / arthropathy**.\n- **Sulfonamides (near term):** **Kernicterus** (displaces bilirubin from albumin).\n- **Chloramphenicol:** **Gray Baby Syndrome** (low UDP-glucuronyl transferase).",
