    "stem": "A 27-year-old woman with rheumatoid arthritis is treated with weekly low-dose methotrexate. She presents to the clinic and discovers that she is 8 weeks pregnant. Methotrexate is immediately discontinued. The genetic counselor discusses the potential teratogenic hazards of first-trimester exposure to folic acid antagonists. What is the enzymatic target of methotrexate, and what constellation of fetal anomalies (aminopterin/methotrexate syndrome) is associated with early in utero exposure?",
