    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "- **Methotrexate & Aminopterin Teratogenicity:**\n  - Methotrexate is a competitive, irreversible **inhibitor of dihydrofolate reductase (DHFR)**.\n  - By inhibiting DHFR, it prevents the conversion of dihydrofolate to tetrahydrofolate ($), halting the synthesis of thymidylate (dTMP) and purines (dGTP, dATP), blocking DNA synthesis, and triggering apoptosis in rapidly dividing embryonic tissues.\n  - **Methotrexate/Aminopterin Syndrome (Folic Acid Antagonist Syndrome):**\n    1. **Craniofacial Malformations:** Craniosynostosis (premature closure of cranial sutures), cloverleaf skull, wide cranial fontanelles, micrognathia, low-set ears, hypertelorism, and **cleft lip / cleft palate**.\n    2. **Central Nervous System Anomalies:** Anencephaly, spina bifida, hydrocephalus, and intellectual disability.\n    3. **Skeletal & Limb Abnormalities:** Limb reduction defects, hypoplastic or absent digits (syndactyly, ectrodactyly), and talipes equinovarus (clubfoot).\n    4. **Growth Deficiency:** Severe intrauterine growth restriction and high rate of spontaneous abortion (hence its clinical use in medical management of ectopic pregnancy).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B) Thymidylate synthase:** Inhibited by 5-fluorouracil (5-FU); renal agenesis is not the classic methotrexate defect.\n  - **(C) Dihydropteroate synthase:** Target of sulfonamides.\n  - **(D) Ribonucleotide reductase:** Target of hydroxyurea.\n  - **(E) Topoisomerase II:** Target of etoposide; sacral agenesis is classic for maternal pregestational diabetes.",
    "pearl": "**Methotrexate in Pregnancy:** Inhibits **Dihydrofolate Reductase (DHFR)** $\nightarrow$ halts DNA synthesis.\nCauses **Aminopterin/Methotrexate Syndrome**: **Craniofacial anomalies (craniosynostosis, cleft palate, micrognathia)**, **neural tube defects**, and **limb/digital hypoplasia**. Also used to terminate **ectopic pregnancy**.",
