    "stem": "A 25-year-old woman with focal epilepsy well-controlled on phenytoin (Dilantin) presents for routine obstetric evaluation after delivering a full-term infant girl. Physical examination of the newborn reveals microcephaly, a wide anterior fontanelle, a broad depressed nasal bridge with hypertelorism, a cleft lip and palate, excessive body hair (hirsutism), and marked hypoplasia of the distal phalanges with tiny, rudimentarily formed fingernails. Cardiac examination reveals a systolic murmur consistent with a ventricular septal defect. What is the diagnosis, and what vitamin must be administered to newborns exposed to maternal phenytoin near delivery?",
