    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "- **Fetal Hydantoin Syndrome (Phenytoin Teratogenicity):**\n  - Phenytoin (Dilantin) is a widely used antiepileptic that blocks voltage-gated sodium channels.\n  - In utero exposure produces **Fetal Hydantoin Syndrome** in up to 10% of exposed fetuses (with milder manifestations in another 30%).\n  - **Classic Phenotypic Features:**\n    1. **Distal Digital Hypoplasia (PATHOGNOMONIC):** **Hypoplastic distal phalanges and rudimentary, small, dysplastic fingernails and toenails**.\n    2. **Craniofacial Dysmorphisms:** Microcephaly, wide prominent fontanelles, **cleft lip and/or cleft palate**, hypertelorism, broad depressed nasal bridge, and low-set ears.\n    3. **Cardiac Anomalies:** Ventricular septal defects (VSD), atrial septal defects (ASD), coarctation of the aorta.\n    4. **Growth & Neurodevelopment:** Pre- and postnatal growth deficiency, mental retardation / developmental delay.\n    5. **Hirsutism:** Coarse, dark facial and body hair.\n- **Neonatal Hemorrhage Risk (Enzyme Induction & Vitamin K Deficiency):**\n  - Phenytoin, carbamazepine, and phenobarbital are potent **inducers of hepatic cytochrome P450 enzymes**.\n  - Accelerated fetal and neonatal hepatic degradation of vitamin K-dependent clotting factors (II, VII, IX, X) drastically increases the risk of **life-threatening neonatal hemorrhage (early hemorrhagic disease of the newborn)** within the first 24 hours of life.\n  - **Prevention:** Oral **Vitamin K supplementation is administered to the mother during the last month of pregnancy**, followed by mandatory **intramuscular Vitamin K1 injection to the newborn immediately at delivery**.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B) Fetal alcohol syndrome:** Characterized by smooth philtrum and thin upper lip, not distal digital hypoplasia.\n  - **(C) Warfarin embryopathy:** Chondrodysplasia punctata and nasal hypoplasia.\n  - **(D) Neonatal lupus:** Congenital complete heart block and annular scaly rash from transplacental anti-Ro/SSA antibodies.\n  - **(E) Zellweger syndrome:** Peroxisomal biogenesis disorder with craniofacial dysmorphism and hypotonia.",
    "pearl": "**Fetal Hydantoin Syndrome (Phenytoin):**\n- **Hypoplastic nails and distal phalanges** (board buzzword!).\n- **Cleft lip / palate**, microcephaly, and **hirsutism**.\n- Induces CYP450 $\nightarrow$ degrades Vitamin K $\nightarrow$ risk of **neonatal bleeding** (must give **Vitamin K at birth**).",
