    "stem": "A 22-year-old unimmunized primigravida at 14 weeks gestation develops acute varicella (chickenpox) with fever and a generalized pruritic vesicular rash in various stages of healing. The infection resolves without maternal pulmonary complications. At 20 weeks gestation, a targeted anatomical ultrasound reveals severe fetal abnormalities: right lower extremity hypoplasia with rudimentary foot, microcephaly, intrauterine growth restriction, and dense echogenic scarring along the right lower extremity. Postnatal evaluation confirms Congenital Varicella Syndrome with characteristic dermatomal, zig-zag cicatricial skin scars and limb hypoplasia. The greatest risk for this congenital syndrome occurs when primary maternal varicella infection is acquired during which gestational interval?",
