    "stem": "A 31-year-old primigravida at 24 weeks gestation presents for routine care. She reports that she recently traveled to a rural tropical region where she sustained multiple mosquito bites and developed a mild illness with a low-grade fever, pruritic maculopapular rash, and bilateral conjunctivitis. Fetal ultrasound reveals profound microcephaly with fetal brain disruption sequence, ventriculomegaly, prominent occipital bone collapse with redundant scalp skin folds, and diffuse subcortical band calcifications. Maternal reverse transcriptase-polymerase chain reaction (RT-PCR) confirms Zika virus infection. What is the vector that transmits this virus, and what is its specific cellular tropism in the developing fetal brain?",
