    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "- **Zika Virus Infection in Pregnancy:**\n  - **Virology & Vector:** Zika virus is a positive-sense, single-stranded, enveloped RNA **flavivirus** transmitted predominantly by the bite of daytime-active **Aedes aegypti (and Aedes albopictus)** mosquitoes. It can also be transmitted **sexually** (persists in semen for months) and vertically from mother to fetus.\n  - **Maternal Presentation:** Often asymptomatic (~80%), or causes a mild illness: low-grade fever, pruritic maculopapular rash, non-purulent **conjunctivitis**, and arthralgias.\n  - **Cellular Tropism & Pathogenesis:**\n    - Zika virus directly targets and infects **cortical neural progenitor cells (NPCs)** in the fetal subventricular zone.\n    - Infection triggers p53-dependent **apoptotic cell death of neural stem cells** and halts cell cycle progression, preventing normal neurogenesis and cortical laminar development.\n  - **Congenital Zika Syndrome (Fetal Brain Disruption Sequence):**\n    1. **Severe Microcephaly:** Often with a collapsed, wrinkled cranial vault and redundant scalp skin folds (\"cutis verticis gyrata\" appearance) due to arrest of brain growth while skull bones continue to collapse.\n    2. **Intracranial Calcifications:** Typically dense, subcortical calcifications at the gray-white matter junction.\n    3. **Ventriculomegaly, Lissencephaly, and Pachygyria:** Smooth brain surface devoid of normal gyri and sulci.\n    4. **Ocular Defects:** Chorioretinal atrophy, optic nerve hypoplasia, and congenital macular scarring.\n    5. **Arthrogryposis:** Severe congenital joint contractures secondary to upper motor neuron loss and fetal akinesia.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Anopheles:** Transmits *Plasmodium* (malaria), not Zika.\n  - **(C) Ixodes tick:** Transmits *Borrelia burgdorferi* (Lyme disease) and *Babesia*.\n  - **(D) Culex mosquito:** Transmits West Nile virus.\n  - **(E) Triatomine bug:** Transmits *Trypanosoma cruzi* (Chagas disease).",
    "pearl": "**Congenital Zika Syndrome:**\n- Virus: **Flavivirus (ssRNA)** transmitted by **Aedes mosquito** or sexual contact.\n- Tropism: Destroys **human neural progenitor cells (NPCs)**.\n- Phenotype: **Severe microcephaly**, collapsed skull with **redundant scalp folds**, subcortical calcifications, **chorioretinal scarring**, and **arthrogryposis** (joint contractures).",
