    "yield_level": "High",
    "stem": "A 30-year-old woman at 29 weeks gestation presents with regular contractions and cervical change. She is diagnosed with preterm labor. Which two medications are given to reduce complications of prematurity, and what are their respective purposes?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Magnesium sulfate for fetal neuroprotection (reducing cerebral palsy risk); betamethasone to enhance fetal lung maturity and reduce respiratory distress syndrome",
      "B": "Magnesium sulfate for lung maturity; betamethasone for neuroprotection according to current guidelines",
      "C": "Both drugs serve the identical purpose of stopping labor permanently under standard diagnostic criteria",
      "D": "Insulin for glucose control and metformin for tocolysis in this clinical context",
      "E": "Neither drug has proven benefit in preterm labor according to current guidelines"
    },
