    "stem": "A 22-year-old woman is diagnosed with a complete hydatidiform mole following a D&C for a presumed miscarriage. The pathology report describes massively swollen, edematous chorionic villi with circumferential trophoblastic proliferation. To definitively differentiate this complete mole from a partial mole, the pathologist performs immunohistochemical staining for the **p57 protein**. What is the expected result of this stain in a complete mole, and what is the underlying genetic principle?",
