    "stem": "A 29-year-old woman presents with light vaginal spotting at 12 weeks gestation. Her uterine size is consistent with her dates. Her serum $\\beta$-hCG is $60,000\\text{ mIU/mL}$ (normal for late first trimester). A transvaginal ultrasound reveals an abnormal, thickened placenta with scattered cystic spaces, alongside a growth-restricted, non-viable fetus. The patient undergoes a D&C. The pathologist notes focal hydropic villi interspersed with normal villi, and nucleated fetal red blood cells are seen within the villous capillaries. What is the most likely karyotype of this conception?",
