    "stem": "A 30-year-old woman is being monitored with weekly $\\beta$-hCG levels following the evacuation of a complete hydatidiform mole. For the first three weeks, her levels steadily declined. However, at weeks 4, 5, and 6, her levels have plateaued at $15,000\\text{ mIU/mL}$ and are now rising. A pelvic ultrasound reveals a solid, highly vascular mass invading deeply into the myometrium. A chest X-ray is perfectly clear with no nodules. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
