    "stem": "A 42-year-old female with a history of chronic hypertension presents to discuss birth control. On examination today, her blood pressure is 162/104 mmHg. She has been taking combined oral contraceptive pills for the past 10 years without any issues and requests a refill. What is the clinical significance of prescribing combined hormonal contraceptives (CHCs) to a patient with uncontrolled hypertension?",
