      "B": "Uncontrolled hypertension (systolic >= 160 mmHg or diastolic >= 100 mmHg) is associated with an up to 10-fold increased risk of myocardial infarction and stroke when combined with the use of estrogen-containing CHCs; therefore, CHCs represent a Category 4 (unacceptable health risk) in this patient.",
      "C": "CHCs will act as a mild vasodilator and help lower her blood pressure, making them a Category 1 option.",
