    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A clinical director at a women's health clinic is updating the institutional guidelines for medical abortion. She is reviewing the maximum gestational age for standard medical abortion and how its efficacy changes across different gestations. According to the provided sources on induced abortion, what is the standard FDA-approved gestational age limit for medical abortion, its comparative efficacy, and how does the Planned Parenthood regimen handle later gestations?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Approved up to 6 weeks gestation; has a 50% efficacy rate; Planned Parenthood regimens do not offer medical abortion after 5 weeks.",
      "B": "Approved up to 10 weeks gestation; efficacy is 97\u201399% up to 49 days (<7 weeks) and decreases to 95\u201398% between 57\u201370 days (8\u201310 weeks); Planned Parenthood utilizes a newer regimen for 9\u201311 weeks that includes a second dose of misoprostol 3\u20136 hours after the first.",
      "C": "Approved up to 14 weeks gestation; efficacy is 99% across all gestations; no dosage adjustments are needed.",
      "D": "Approved up to 24 weeks gestation; efficacy is 75%; and it requires co-administration of systemic antibiotics and low-dose heparin.",
      "E": "Approved up to 12 weeks gestation; but it must be performed in a surgical operating room due to a 20% risk of immediate catastrophic uterine hemorrhage."
    },
    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "days (<7 weeks) and decreases to 95\u201398% between 57\u201370 days (8\u201310 weeks); Planned 353 Parenthood utilizes a newer regimen for 9\u201311 weeks that includes a second dose of misoprostol 3\u20136 hours after the first. \u25cf  A. Approved up to 6 weeks gestation; has a 50% efficacy rate; Planned Parenthood regimens do not offer medical abortion after 5 weeks.  -  Incorrect  . Medical abortion is highly effective (>95%) and approved well beyond 6 weeks. \u25cf  B. Approved up to 10 weeks gestation; efficacy is 97\u201399% up to 49 days (<7 weeks) and decreases to 95\u201398% between 57\u201370 days (8\u201310 weeks); Planned Parenthood utilizes a newer regimen for 9\u201311 weeks that includes a second dose of misoprostol 3\u20136 hours after the first.  -  Correct  .  Standard medical abortion (Mifepristone + Misoprostol) is FDA-approved for use up to  10 weeks (70 days) of gestation  . Its efficacy is highly dependent on gestational  age:  97\u201399% effective up to 49 days (<7 weeks)  and decreasing slightly to  95\u201398%  between 57\u201370 days (8\u201310 weeks)  . To extend this option safely, Planned Parenthood  has adopted a newer regimen for pregnancies between 9\u201311 weeks, which incorporates a second dose of mifepristone/misoprostol or a modified dosing schedule. \u25cf  C. Approved up to 14 weeks gestation; efficacy is 99% across all gestations; no dosage adjustments are needed.  -  Incorrect  . The standard  medical limit is 10 weeks, and efficacy declines with increasing gestational age. \u25cf  D. Approved up to 24 weeks gestation; efficacy is 75%; and it requires co-administration of systemic antibiotics and low-dose heparin.  -  Incorrect  . Medical abortion is not used as a standalone outpatient regimen up to 24 weeks; second-trimester terminations require surgical D&E or inpatient labor induction. \u25cf  E. Approved up to 12 weeks gestation; but it must be performed in a surgical operating room due to a 20% risk of immediate catastrophic uterine hemorrhage.  - Incorrect  . Medical abortion is safe for home administration  and does not require an operating room. The risk of major hemorrhage is extremely low.",
