      "B": "Complications are rare and relate to gestational age; medical abortion is associated with slightly more bleeding and retained tissues than surgical; and rigorous scientific evidence demonstrates that induced abortion does NOT increase the risk of subsequent infertility, ectopic pregnancy, preterm delivery, cervical insufficiency, breast cancer, or depression.",
      "C": "Medical abortion has a 90% rate of severe infection, while first-trimester surgical abortion has a 10% rate of uterine perforation.",
      "D": "Both medical and surgical abortions cause a permanent increase in the risk of subsequent preterm delivery due to systemic oxytocin receptor downregulation.",
