    "stem": "A health policy analyst is reviewing the global and national landscape of abortion regulations and safety. She compiles a report summarizing the legal framework in the United States following recent Supreme Court decisions, alongside WHO data on unsafe abortions. Which of the following statements is correct regarding the global impact of unsafe abortions and the current legal status of abortion in the United States?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Globally, unsafe abortions are virtually non-existent due to strict WHO enforcement; and the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision remains the active, overriding federal law protecting abortion rights in all 50 U.S. states.",
      "B": "Globally, approximately 45% of all induced abortions are unsafe (typically performed by untrained persons or using dangerous methods), with 5\u201313% of maternal deaths attributed to them; in the U.S., the 2022 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Association decision overruled Roe v. Wade, giving individual states the power to regulate abortion, and induced abortion remains legal in New York.",
      "C": "Unsafe abortions account for 90% of all maternal deaths globally; in the U.S., the Dobbs decision made induced abortion a federal crime punishable by up to 10 years in prison across all states.",
      "D": "Globally, unsafe abortions have the highest rates in Western Europe and North America; and abortion is strictly illegal under all circumstances in the state of New York.",
      "E": "Unsafe abortions are defined strictly as medical abortions performed after 6 weeks; in the U.S., Roe v. Wade was upheld in 2022, expanding federal abortion access to the third trimester."
    },
    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "(typically performed by untrained persons or using dangerous methods), with 5\u201313% of maternal deaths attributed to them; in the U.S., the 2022 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Association decision overruled Roe v. Wade, giving individual states the power to regulate abortion, and induced abortion remains legal in New York. \u25cf  A. Globally, unsafe abortions are virtually non-existent due to strict WHO enforcement; and the 1973 Roe v. Wade decision remains the active, overriding federal law protecting abortion rights in all 50 U.S. states.  -  Incorrect  . Unsafe abortions are a major global health issue. Roe v. Wade was overruled in 2022 by the Dobbs decision. \u25cf  B. Globally, approximately 45% of all induced abortions are unsafe (typically performed by untrained persons or using dangerous methods), with 5\u201313% of maternal deaths attributed to them; in the U.S., the 2022 Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Association decision overruled Roe v. Wade, giving individual states the power to regulate abortion, and induced abortion remains legal in New York.  -  Correct  . According to the WHO,  45% of all  induced abortions globally are unsafe  , often performed by untrained individuals using  invasive or toxic methods, leading to approximately 7 million hospitalizations and accounting for  5\u201313% of maternal deaths  . In the United States, the legal landscape  shifted dramatically in 2022 with the  Dobbs v. Jackson Women's Health Association  Supreme Court ruling  , which overruled both  Roe v. Wade  (1973) and  Planned  Parenthood v. Casey  (1992), returning the authority to regulate or ban abortion to individual states. Induced abortion remains fully legal in New York. \u25cf  C. Unsafe abortions account for 90% of all maternal deaths globally; in the U.S., the Dobbs decision made induced abortion a federal crime punishable by up to 10 years in prison across all states.  -  Incorrect  . Unsafe  abortions account for 5\u201313% (not 90%) of maternal deaths. The Dobbs decision did not establish a federal criminal ban; it left regulation to individual states. \u25cf  D. Globally, unsafe abortions have the highest rates in Western Europe and North America; and abortion is strictly illegal under all circumstances in the state of New York.  -  Incorrect  . Unsafe abortions are concentrated  in developing regions (such as South/Central Asia, Africa, and Latin America) where legal restrictions and lack of healthcare access exist. Abortion is legal in New York. \u25cf  E. Unsafe abortions are defined strictly as medical abortions performed after 6 weeks; in the U.S., Roe v. Wade was upheld in 2022, expanding federal abortion access to the third trimester.  -  Incorrect  . Unsafe abortions are defined by WHO based 356 on the lack of safety/training of the provider. Roe v. Wade was overruled, not expanded or upheld, in 2022. 357 Prompt Every source is a full lecture (these are the entire presentations, not excerpts) that will be included on our upcoming US MD in-house reproductive systems exam. Our school has a policy that every question must test on a detail that falls within the scope of at least one of the lecture's learning objectives. Please generate an applied, representative STEP 1-style (A Step 1\u2013style question is a clinical vignette-based multiple-choice question that tests application of basic science concepts in a medical context. It presents a short patient scenario with relevant and irrelevant details, followed by a single best-answer question that requires identifying the underlying mechanism, diagnosis, or next step.) practice exam with 20 A-E multiple choice questions per source (i will tell you which sources) to test my mastery of the material ahead of the exam. The distractors must be common misconceptions. Each question set should only test on information discretely from the corresponding lecture, do not test on outside material. When a source lists lecture objectives, key points, etc., make sure that the question set covers them comprehensively . The idea is that if someone were to score a 100% on a given lecture\u2019 s associated 20-question practice set, it should imply that they have a high level of mastery over the important material in preparation for the exam. In terms of formatting, please break the practice exam up by session (source). only reveal answers in the form of an answer key section at the end of each set of questions. The answer key should give the answer as well as explain why that answer is correct, and why each incorrect answer is wrong. explain conceptually and fully , but in a way that makes sense and allows the reader to learn from it. As for the questions, remember to include 2 line breaks between each answer choice, as well as 2 line breaks in the answer keys between questions. Randomize the A-E correct answer distribution, making sure it is not predictable. Also do NOT use any latex formatting. use the source \"8.1 1 Endo W eek 3 Notebook Qs - Google Docs.pdf\" as a reference for the formatting style i am looking for , as well as for the way i want the answer keys to be structured. Let's begin with Set 1, for the lecture \"[Fillable PDF] IMC 534 - Female Reproductive Histology W orkbook.pdf\". 20 questions, numbered 1-20. include the answer key at the end of the set",
