    "yield_level": "Mid",
    "stem": "A 22-year-old woman presents to her gynecologist complaining of painless bumps on her vulva that she noticed two weeks ago. She has a new sexual partner. Physical examination reveals multiple soft, fleshy, cauliflower-like, verrucous papules on the labia majora and the perineum. The lesions are painless and do not bleed when touched. A biopsy of one of the lesions is performed to confirm the diagnosis. Which of the following histologic findings is the absolute hallmark of this specific infection?",
