    "stem": "A 4-month-old infant is brought to the pediatrician by his mother because he has developed a weak cry, chronic hoarseness, and occasional stridor (noisy breathing). The mother reports that she had extensive genital warts during her pregnancy and delivered the baby vaginally. Direct laryngoscopy of the infant reveals multiple, small, raspberry-like growths on the true vocal cords. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
