    "stem": "A 24-year-old man presents to the clinic with intense itching in his pubic region for the past week. The itching is much worse at night. Physical examination reveals several tiny, 2-mm, pale-bluish macules on the skin of his lower abdomen and pubic area. Upon close inspection of the pubic hair with a magnifying glass, the physician observes tiny, crab-like organisms clinging tightly to the base of the hair shafts, along with small white oval structures firmly cemented to the hair. Which of the following is the most appropriate first-line treatment for this condition?",
