    "stem": "A 28-year-old pregnant woman, newly diagnosed with HIV at 14 weeks gestation, is referred to a high-risk obstetrician. Her CD4 count is 450 cells/$\\mu$L, and her viral load is 50,000 copies/mL. She is extremely anxious about transmitting the virus to her unborn child. Which of the following is the most critical and effective intervention to reduce the risk of perinatal (vertical) transmission of HIV from this mother to her fetus?",
