    "stem": "A 32-year-old woman with a history of HIV presents for a routine checkup. She has been non-compliant with her ART regimen for the past 2 years. Her most recent lab results show a viral load of 250,000 copies/mL and a CD4+ T-cell count of 180 cells/$\\mu$L. Based on her current immunologic status, she is at immediate risk for a life-threatening pneumonia caused by an opportunistic fungal pathogen. Which of the following medications must be prescribed today as primary prophylaxis against this specific organism?",
