    "stem": "A neonate is born to an HIV-positive mother whose viral load was consistently undetectable throughout her pregnancy due to strict adherence to her ART regimen. The infant appears healthy and vigorous at birth. To further minimize the risk of vertical transmission, standard pediatric protocol dictates that the infant receives post-exposure prophylaxis. Which of the following is the standard prophylactic regimen for a low-risk neonate born to a well-controlled HIV-positive mother?",
