    "rationale": "- **Clinical Presentation:** The triad of severe **microcephaly**, periventricular/intracranial calcifications, and a history of travel to an endemic area (South America/Brazil) is the absolute hallmark of **Congenital Zika Syndrome**.\n- **Microbiology:** The Zika virus is a Flavivirus (an enveloped, ss(+) RNA virus). \n- **Transmission:** \n  - It is an arbovirus (arthropod-borne). The primary vector is the **Aedes aegypti mosquito** (the same mosquito that transmits Dengue and Yellow Fever). \n  - *(Crucially for a repro block, Zika is unique among arboviruses because it can ALSO be transmitted sexually in human semen, meaning pregnant women whose partners travel to endemic areas are at risk).*\n- **Pathogenesis:** The virus crosses the placenta, specifically targets neural progenitor cells in the developing fetal brain, and destroys them via apoptosis, resulting in severe brain destruction, calcification, and a collapsed, small skull (microcephaly).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Unpasteurized dairy:** *Listeria monocytogenes* (causes meningitis/sepsis/stillbirth, not classic microcephaly with calcifications).\n  - **(B) Respiratory droplets:** Rubella or CMV (CMV causes periventricular calcifications and microcephaly, but Zika is the classic epidemic cause tied to recent tropical travel).\n  - **(D) Cat feces:** *Toxoplasma gondii* (causes diffuse intracranial calcifications, hydrocephalus, chorioretinitis).\n  - **(E) Dog saliva:** Rabies virus.",
    "pearl": "The **Zika virus** (transmitted by the **Aedes mosquito** and sexually) targets fetal neural progenitor cells, causing profound congenital **microcephaly** and intracranial calcifications.",
