    "stem": "A 30-year-old man who has sex with men (MSM) is diagnosed with Lymphogranuloma Venereum (LGV) proctitis, presenting with severe rectal pain, tenesmus, and purulent bloody rectal discharge. The physician plans to prescribe the first-line pharmacologic treatment to eradicate the intracellular bacteria causing this deep lymphatic infection. Which of the following is the most appropriate antibiotic regimen?",
