    "stem": "A 26-year-old woman who is 4 weeks postpartum and exclusively breastfeeding her newborn presents to the clinic with a 2-day history of a painful, swollen, and red right breast. She also reports fevers and chills. Her temperature is $102.0^\\circ\\text{F}$. Physical examination reveals a wedge-shaped area of erythema, induration, and exquisite tenderness in the upper outer quadrant of the right breast. There is no fluctuant mass. Which of the following is the most appropriate management regarding her infant's feeding?",
