    "stem": "A 65-year-old woman is diagnosed with an ER+/PR+ invasive ductal carcinoma. She is started on an aromatase inhibitor (Anastrozole) to prevent recurrence. Which of the following is the most significant adverse effect of this medication that requires routine clinical monitoring?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Endometrial hyperplasia and cancer",
      "B": "Deep vein thrombosis (DVT) and pulmonary embolism",
      "C": "Severe osteoporosis and bone fractures",
      "D": "Dilated cardiomyopathy",
      "E": "Hemorrhagic cystitis"
    },
    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "- **Pharmacology of Breast Cancer:** \n  - **Aromatase Inhibitors (Anastrozole, Letrozole, Exemestane):** These drugs work by blocking the aromatase enzyme, completely stopping the peripheral production of estrogen in adipose tissue. They are the drug of choice for ER+ breast cancer in **postmenopausal** women.\n- **The Adverse Effect:** By utterly depleting the body of all remaining estrogen, these drugs induce a profound state of estrogen deprivation. Estrogen is critical for maintaining bone density (it inhibits osteoclasts). Therefore, the most significant side effect of aromatase inhibitors is severe **osteoporosis** and an increased risk of bone fractures. Patients require routine DEXA scans and often bisphosphonate therapy.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Endometrial cancer & (B) DVT/PE:** These are the classic, feared side effects of **Tamoxifen** (a SERM used in *premenopausal* women). Tamoxifen acts as an antagonist in the breast but as an *agonist* in the endometrium and liver (increasing clotting factors). Aromatase inhibitors have NO estrogenic agonist activity, so they do NOT cause endometrial cancer or clots.\n  - **(D) Cardiomyopathy:** Classic side effect of Trastuzumab (Herceptin) and Doxorubicin.\n  - **(E) Hemorrhagic cystitis:** Side effect of Cyclophosphamide.",
    "pearl": "**Aromatase inhibitors** (Anastrozole) cause profound estrogen depletion, leading to **osteoporosis** and bone fractures.\n**Tamoxifen** causes **endometrial cancer** and **DVT/PE** because it acts as an estrogen agonist in the uterus and liver.",
