    "stem": "A 58-year-old woman undergoes a screening mammogram, which is unremarkable. However, on physical examination, her physician notes a subtle architectural distortion and a vague thickening in the left breast. A biopsy is performed. The pathologist sees a proliferation of small, uniform, monomorphic malignant cells infiltrating through the stroma. The cells are lined up perfectly one after the other in a \"single-file\" pattern. There is no gland formation and no desmoplastic stromal response. The loss of which specific cellular protein is responsible for this unique pattern of invasion?",
