    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A pathologist is examining an ovarian resection specimen from a 44-year-old female. Grossly, the mass is a large, unilocular, multicystic structure measuring 15 cm, filled with glistening, thick mucinous fluid and divided by delicate, translucent fibrous septa. Under light microscopy, the cysts are lined by a single layer of tall, column-shaped epithelial cells with abundant intracellular mucin and basally located, uniform nuclei, without cytological atypia or stromal invasion. What is the diagnosis, how common are primary malignant versions of this tumor compared to serous carcinomas, and what clinical entity is often confused with it?",
