    "rationale": "carcinomas are rare (<5% of all ovarian cancers), and the vast majority of mucinous tumors (80%) are benign or borderline; and metastatic mucinous carcinomas from the appendix or GI tract (which can present as pseudomyxoma peritonei with bilateral ovarian involvement) can easily mimic or be confused with primary ovarian mucinous tumors. \u25cf  A. Primary mucinous cystadenocarcinoma; it is the most common malignant ovarian tumor; and it is easily confused with a dysgerminoma. - Incorrect. Serous carcinoma is the most common ovarian malignancy , and mucinous cystadenomas are benign, as characterized by lack of atypia or invasion. \u25cf  B. Benign mucinous cystadenoma; primary ovarian mucinous carcinomas are rare (<5% of all ovarian cancers), and the vast majority of mucinous tumors (80%) are benign or borderline; and metastatic mucinous carcinomas from the appendix or GI tract (which can present as pseudomyxoma peritonei with bilateral ovarian involvement) can easily mimic or be confused with primary ovarian mucinous tumors. - Correct. This is a classic benign mucinous cystadenoma (multilocular , filled with glistening mucinous fluid, lined by a single layer of tall columnar mucinous epithelium without atypia or invasion). Primaries are rare (<5%), and 80% of ovarian mucinous neoplasms are benign or borderline. Importantly , metastatic mucinous cancers (most classically from the appendix, colon, or stomach) frequently metastasize to both ovaries, presenting as bilateral complex masses that can mimic a primary ovarian mucinous carcinoma and cause pseudomyxoma peritonei. \u25cf  C. Endometrioid adenocarcinoma; it is more common than serous tumors; and it is easily confused with a follicular cyst. - Incorrect. Endometrioid tumors are not mucinous, and serous tumors are more common. \u25cf  D. Brenner tumor; it is always highly malignant; and it is easily confused with Meigs' syndrome. - Incorrect. Brenner tumors are epithelial tumors consisting of urothelial-like nests, and are almost always benign. \u25cf  E. Yolk sac tumor; it is benign; and it is easily confused with a mature cystic teratoma. - Incorrect. Y olk sac tumors are highly malignant germ cell tumors, not benign mucinous tumors.",
