      "C": "BRCA1 mutation carriers have a lifetime breast cancer risk of approximately 72% and a lifetime ovarian cancer risk of approximately 44%, with risk-reducing bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy (BSO) recommended by age 35 to 40 (after childbearing is complete); BRCA2 carriers have a breast cancer risk of approximately 69% and an ovarian cancer risk of approximately 17%, with BSO recommended by age 40 to 45.",
