    "stem": "A 56-year-old female G0 presents with abdominal bloating and early satiety. CT of the abdomen and pelvis reveals bilateral heterogeneous ovarian masses, a large omental mass (\"omental caking\"), and a significant volume of ascites. Washings, a total abdominal hysterectomy, bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy (TAH/BSO), omentectomy, and cytoreductive debulking are performed. Pathology confirms a high-grade papillary serous carcinoma with peritoneal metastases on the liver surface, consistent with Stage III disease. According to ACOG and ASCCP guidelines, what is the standard chemotherapy regimen for this patient, and what is the typical 5-year survival rate for Stage III ovarian cancer?",
