    "rationale": "PIK3CA; and it is associated with endometriosis and L ynch syndrome (HNPCC). \u25cf  A. High-grade serous carcinoma; mutated in TP53 and BRCA1; associated with Hereditary Breast and Ovarian Cancer (HBOC) syndrome. - Incorrect. High-grade serous carcinoma does not typically feature sheets of clear cells and hobnail cells. \u25cf  B. Mucinous cystadenocarcinoma; mutated in Kras and HER2; associated with Peutz-Jeghers syndrome. - Incorrect. Mucinous cancers have tall mucin-producing cells, not glycogen-rich clear cytoplasm with hobnailing. \u25cf  C. Clear cell carcinoma of the ovary; mutated in ARID1A or PIK3CA; and it is associated with endometriosis and L ynch syndrome (HNPCC). - Correct. Clear cell carcinoma of the ovary is a T ype I epithelial malignancy characterized histologically by sheets or glands of cells with abundant, glycogen-rich clear cytoplasm, and distinctive \"hobnail\" cells (atypical cells whose large nuclei bulge prominently into the gland lumen). It is highly associated with ovarian endometriosis and is a classic ovarian cancer associated with L ynch syndrome (HNPCC), demonstrating somatic mutations in ARID1A or PIK3CA. \u25cf  D. Granulosa cell tumor; mutated in FOXL2; associated with McCune-Albright syndrome. - Incorrect. Granulosa cell tumors have cof fee-bean nuclei and Call-Exner bodies, not clear hobnail cells. \u25cf  E. Dysgerminoma; mutated in KIT ; associated with Swyer syndrome. - Incorrect. Dysgerminomas also have clear cells, but they have thin fibrous septa with lymphocytes and lack the diagnostic \"hobnail\" cell morphology or association with endometriosis.",
