    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 29-year-old female is undergoing beta-hCG monitoring following suction curettage of a complete hydatidiform mole. Her weekly beta-hCG levels over the past month are as follows: Week 1: 4,500 mIU/mL, Week 2: 4,350 mIU/mL, Week 3: 4,450 mIU/mL, Week 4: 4,400 mIU/mL. According to the FIGO/ACOG criteria, what is the clinical significance of these findings, and what is the next step in management?",
