      "B": "Placental Site Trophoblastic Tumor (PSTT); arises from intermediate trophoblasts of the placental site (anchoring villi); it characteristically expresses hPL on immunohistochemistry and is associated with only mildly elevated serum beta-hCG, unlike the massive beta-hCG elevations typical of choriocarcinoma.",
