    "stem": "A pathologist is reviewing a slide of a rare gestational trophoblastic neoplasm from a 36-year-old female. Microscopically, the tumor is composed of nests and cords of uniform, epithelioid intermediate trophoblasts surrounded by a prominent, hyalinized, eosinophilic extracellular matrix resembling keratin, mimicking a squamous cell carcinoma. The cells are positive for p63 and GATA3 on immunohistochemistry. 292 What is the name of this tumor, what cells does it arise from, and how is it clinically managed?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Placental site trophoblastic tumor; arises from cytotrophoblasts; treated primarily with methotrexate.",
      "B": "Choriocarcinoma; arises from syncytiotrophoblasts; treated primarily with pelvic radiation.",
      "C": "Brenner tumor; arises from transitional cells of the urothelium; treated with ciprofloxacin.",
      "D": "Epithelioid Trophoblastic Tumor (ETT); arises from neoplastic chorionic-type intermediate trophoblasts; it behaves similarly to PSTT, is relatively chemoresistant, and is primarily treated with surgical resection (hysterectomy).",
      "E": "Dysgerminoma; arises from pluripotential germ cells; treated with platinum-based chemotherapy."
    },
    "correct": "D",
    "rationale": "chorionic-type intermediate trophoblasts; it behaves similarly to PSTT, is relatively chemoresistant, and is primarily treated with surgical resection (hysterectomy). \u25cf  A. Placental site trophoblastic tumor; arises from cytotrophoblasts; treated primarily with methotrexate.  -  Incorrect  . PSTT does  not show this classic squamous-like nests surrounded by hyalinized eosinophilic matrix, and is treated with hysterectomy (not methotrexate). \u25cf  B. Choriocarcinoma; arises from syncytiotrophoblasts; treated primarily with pelvic radiation.  -  Incorrect  . Choriocarcinoma is  treated primarily with chemotherapy, and lacks the squamous/epithelioid-like hyalinized pattern of ETT. \u25cf  C. Brenner tumor; arises from transitional cells of the urothelium; treated with ciprofloxacin.  -  Incorrect  . Brenner tumor of the ovary  is typically a benign, asymptomatic epithelial neoplasm, not a malignant gestational trophoblastic neoplasm of the uterine wall. \u25cf  D. Epithelioid Trophoblastic Tumor (ETT); arises from neoplastic chorionic-type intermediate trophoblasts; it behaves similarly to PSTT, is relatively chemoresistant, and is primarily treated with surgical resection (hysterectomy).  - Correct  . Epithelioid Trophoblastic Tumor (ETT) is  a rare gestational trophoblastic disease arising from neoplastic  chorionic-type intermediate  trophoblasts  . Under light microscopy, it features nests and cords of uniform epithelioid cells surrounded by a highly characteristic, prominent,  hyalinized, eosinophilic  extracellular matrix resembling keratin  , which mimics a squamous cell carcinoma.  ETT cells are positive 306 for p63 and GATA3 on immunohistochemistry. Like PSTT, ETT is relatively chemoresistant and is primarily treated with surgical resection (hysterectomy). \u25cf  E. Dysgerminoma; arises from pluripotential germ cells; treated with platinum-based chemotherapy.  -  Incorrect  . Dysgerminoma  is an ovarian germ cell tumor, not a uterine intermediate trophoblastic neoplasm.",
