    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 22-year-old medical student is studying for his first embryology exam. He is reviewing the transition from a bilaminar disc to a trilaminar embryo. How is the process of gastrulation defined, during which week of development does it occur, and what is its initiating structural landmark?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Gastrulation is the transition from a trilaminar disc to a 4-layered fetus during Week 5, initiated by the closure of the neural tube.",
      "B": "Gastrulation is the division of the zygote into a morula during Week 1, initiated by the acrosome reaction.",
      "C": "Gastrulation is the formation of the amniotic cavity during Week 4, initiated by the decidualization of the stroma.",
      "D": "Gastrulation is the division of the trophoblast into cytotrophoblasts and syncytiotrophoblasts during Week 2, initiated by blastocyst hatching.",
      "E": "Gastrulation is the process by which the bilaminar embryonic disc develops into a tri-layered embryonic disc (ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm) during Week 3, initiated by the formation of the primitive streak on the surface of the epiblast."
    },
    "correct": "E",
    "rationale": "develops into a tri-layered embryonic disc (ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm) during Week 3, initiated by the formation of the primitive streak on the surface of the epiblast. A. Gastrulation is the transition from a trilaminar disc to a 4-layered fetus during Week 5, initiated by the closure of the neural tube.: Incorrect. Gastrulation occurs in Week 3 and converts a bilaminar disc into a trilaminar embryo. B. Gastrulation is the division of the zygote into a morula during Week 1, initiated by the acrosome reaction.: Incorrect. This describes early cleavage, not gastrulation. C. Gastrulation is the formation of the amniotic cavity during Week 4, initiated by the decidualization of the stroma.: Incorrect. Amniotic cavity formation occurs on Day 8 (Week 2). 322 D. Gastrulation is the division of the trophoblast into cytotrophoblasts and syncytiotrophoblasts during Week 2, initiated by blastocyst hatching.: Incorrect. This is trophoblast differentiation during early implantation, not gastrulation. E. Gastrulation is the process by which the bilaminar embryonic disc develops into a tri-layered embryonic disc (ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm) during Week 3, initiated by the formation of the primitive streak on the surface of the epiblast.: Correct. Gastrulation occurs during Week 3 of development. It is the process by which the bilaminar embryonic disc is converted into a tri-layered (trilaminar) embryonic disc composed of three germ layers: ectoderm, mesoderm, and endoderm. This process is initiated by the formation of the primitive streak on the caudal surface of the epiblast.",
    "pearl": "",
    "learning_objectives": []
