    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "An obstetrician is examining a placenta and umbilical cord immediately following an uncomplicated vaginal delivery. She notes the spiral structure of the cord and counts the vessels within the cut surface. Based on the Placentation and Umbilical Cord slides, what are the normal vessels and structural features of the umbilical cord at birth, and when does its precursor begin to form?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "It contains 1 artery and 2 veins surrounded by amniotic fluid, and begins to form during Week 8 of development.",
      "B": "It contains 2 arteries and 1 vein embedded within protective Wharton's jelly, and begins to form during Week 3 when the connecting stalk and allantois assemble.",
      "C": "It contains 2 veins and 2 arteries surrounded by embryonic mesoderm, and begins to form during the 1st week.",
      "D": "It contains 1 artery and 1 vein surrounded by the chorionic plate, and begins to form during Week 5.",
      "E": "It contains 3 arteries and no veins, and is composed of pure syncytiotrophoblast cells that form on Day 5."
    },
    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "Wharton's jelly, and begins to form during Week 3 when the connecting stalk and allantois assemble. A. It contains 1 artery and 2 veins surrounded by amniotic fluid, and begins to form during Week 8 of development.: Incorrect. The umbilical cord contains 2 arteries and 1 vein (reversing the numbers in this option), and begins forming earlier than Week 8. B. It contains 2 arteries and 1 vein embedded within protective Wharton's jelly, and begins to form during Week 3 when the connecting stalk and allantois assemble.: Correct. The umbilical cord normally contains three vessels: two umbilical arteries (which carry deoxygenated fetal blood to the placenta) and one umbilical vein (which carries oxygenated blood from the placenta to the fetus). These vessels are cushioned and protected from compression by Wharton's jelly. Its precursor begins to form in Week 3 when the connecting stalk and allantois assemble. C. It contains 2 veins and 2 arteries surrounded by embryonic mesoderm, and begins to form during the 1st week.: Incorrect. The umbilical cord contains 2 arteries and 1 vein, and does not begin to assemble in the first week. D. It contains 1 artery and 1 vein surrounded by the chorionic plate, and begins to form during Week 5.: Incorrect. The umbilical cord contains three vessels and begins its assembly in Week 3. E. It contains 3 arteries and no veins, and is composed of pure syncytiotrophoblast cells that form on Day 5.: Incorrect. The cord has 2 arteries and 1 vein, is filled with Wharton's jelly, and begins forming as a connecting stalk in Week 3.",
