    "qnum": 256,
    "topic": "Gametogenesis, Fertilization, & (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A pediatric neurosurgeon is operating on an 8-year-old child with a craniopharyngioma, a benign brain tumor located in the suprasellar region. She explains to the parents that this tumor arises from remnants of Rathke's pouch. According to the embryologic derivatives tables, what is the germ layer of origin of Rathke's pouch (adenohypophysis), and what other tissues share this same surface ectoderm origin?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Neural tube; brain, spinal cord, and neurohypophysis.",
      "B": "Mesoderm; skeletal muscle, kidneys, and ovaries.",
      "C": "Endoderm; lung epithelium, liver, and thyroid follicular cells.",
      "D": "Surface ectoderm; epidermis, adenohypophysis (from Rathke pouch), lens of eye, epithelial linings of oral cavity, sensory organs of ear, olfactory epithelium, anal canal below pectinate line, and parotid, sweat, and mammary glands.",
      "E": "Neural crest; melanocytes, Schwann cells, and adrenal medulla."
    },
    "correct": "D",
    "rationale": "pouch), lens of eye, epithelial linings of oral cavity, sensory organs of ear, olfactory epithelium, anal canal below pectinate line, and parotid, sweat, and mammary glands. A. Neural tube; brain, spinal cord, and neurohypophysis.: Incorrect. Brain, spinal cord, and neurohypophysis arise from neuroectoderm (neural tube), not surface ectoderm. B. Mesoderm; skeletal muscle, kidneys, and ovaries.: Incorrect. These are mesodermal derivatives. C. Endoderm; lung epithelium, liver, and thyroid follicular cells.: Incorrect. These are endodermal derivatives. D. Surface ectoderm; epidermis, adenohypophysis (from Rathke pouch), lens of eye, epithelial linings of oral cavity, sensory organs of ear, olfactory epithelium, anal canal below pectinate line, and parotid, sweat, and mammary glands.: Correct. The adenohypophysis (anterior pituitary) develops from Rathke's pouch, which is an invagination of the embryonic oral cavity ectoderm. According to the First Aid tables, Rathke's pouch and the adenohypophysis are derived from the surface ectoderm. Other surface ectoderm derivatives include: the epidermis, the lens of the 326 eye, epithelial linings of the oral cavity, sensory organs of the ear, olfactory epithelium, anal canal below the pectinate line, and parotid, sweat, and mammary glands. E. Neural crest; melanocytes, Schwann cells, and adrenal medulla.: Incorrect. These are neural crest derivatives, not surface ectoderm.",
