    "rationale": "the VACTERL association); the postnatal remnant of the embryonic notochord is the nucleus pulposus of the intervertebral disc. A. Ectoderm; spinal cord.: Incorrect. Ectoderm defects are not the primary cause of VACTERL association, and the spinal cord is derived from the neural tube, not the notochord. B. Mesoderm (noting that mesodermal defects are associated with the VACTERL association); the postnatal remnant of the embryonic notochord is the nucleus pulposus of the intervertebral disc.: Correct. According to the First Aid table, defects in the development of the embryonic mesoderm germ layer are associated with the VACTERL association (Vertebral defects, Anal atresia, Cardiac defects, Tracheo-Esophageal fistula, Renal defects, and Limb defects). Additionally, the tables note that while the notochord is a mesodermal structure that induces the overlying ectoderm to form the neural plate, its only postnatal structural derivative is the nucleus pulposus of the intervertebral disc. C. Endoderm; the postnatal remnant of the embryonic notochord is Meckel's diverticulum.: Incorrect. Meckel's diverticulum is a vitelline duct remnant, not a notochord remnant, and the notochord does not derive from endoderm. D. Neural crest; the postnatal remnant of the embryonic notochord is the Schwann cell myelin sheath.: Incorrect. Schwann cells are derived from the neural crest, but they are not a remnant of the embryonic notochord. E. Ectoderm; the postnatal remnant of the embryonic notochord is the craniopharyngioma.: Incorrect. Craniopharyngioma is a tumor of Rathke's pouch (surface ectoderm), not a notochord remnant.",
