    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "(which forms the dermis of the dorsal body region), and Myotome (which forms the trunk and limb musculature). A. Sclerotome (which forms the vertebrae and ribs), Dermatome (which forms the dermis of the dorsal body region), and Myotome (which forms the trunk and limb musculature).: Correct. Paraxial mesoderm segments to form somites. The First Aid diagram outlines the division of a somite into three distinct sub-layers: (1) Sclerotome (which forms the vertebrae and ribs); (2) Dermatome (which forms the dermis of the dorsal body region); and (3) Myotome (which forms the trunk and limb musculature). B. Notochord (which forms the spinal cord), Somite (which forms the gonads), and Splanchnopleuric mesoderm (which forms the heart).: Incorrect. Notochord does not form the spinal cord (it induces it), and splanchnic mesoderm forms the cardiovascular system but is not a somite subdivision. C. Epiblast (which forms the amnion), Hypoblast (which forms the yolk sac), and Syncytiotrophoblast (which forms the chorionic plate).: Incorrect. These are early blastocyst and bilaminar disc tissues, not somite subdivisions. D. Intermediate mesoderm (which forms the kidneys), Lateral plate mesoderm (which forms the gut tube), and Ectoderm (which forms the nails).: Incorrect. These represent separate, broad germ layer divisions rather than divisions of a single paraxial somite. E. Ectoderm (which forms the CNS), Endoderm (which forms the lungs), and Mesoderm (which forms the blood vessels).: Incorrect. These are the three primary germ layers, not subdivisions of a somite. 328",
