    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "and carries no increased risk of breast carcinoma. \u25cf  A. Columnar cell change; carries a 4-to-5-fold increased risk of invasive ductal carcinoma.  -  Incorrect  . Columnar cell change is characterized  by tall columnar cells, and does not carry a 4-to-5-fold risk. \u25cf  B. Apocrine metaplasia; it is a benign feature of fibrocystic change and carries no increased risk of breast carcinoma.  -  Correct  . Apocrine  metaplasia is a classic histopathologic finding in fibrocystic breast changes. It is characterized by luminal epithelial cells that have undergone metaplasia to resemble apocrine sweat gland cells, demonstrating abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm, apical snouts (secretory projections), and small, dark, round nuclei. This metaplastic change is entirely benign and carries no increased risk of developing breast carcinoma. 191 \u25cf  C. Ductal epithelial hyperplasia with atypia; carries a 1.5-to-2-fold increased risk of breast cancer.  -  Incorrect  . Epithelial hyperplasia  with atypia (such as ADH) carries a 4-to-5-fold risk, and does not match the apocrine metaplasia description. \u25cf  D. Sclerosing adenosis; carries a 10-fold increased risk of bilateral breast cancer.  - Incorrect  . Sclerosing adenosis carries a \"possible\"  slightly increased risk (approx. 1.5-fold) of cancer, not a 10-fold risk. \u25cf  E. Atypical lobular hyperplasia; carries a 20-30% absolute lifetime risk of developing invasive lobular carcinoma.  -  Incorrect  .  This describes LCIS risk, not apocrine metaplasia.",
    "pearl": "",
