    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "accompanied by increased stromal cellularity, stromal nuclear atypia, and increased mitotic figures. \u25cf  A. Her premenopausal status, the mobility of the mass, and presence of multiple blue-domed cysts on gross examination.  -  Incorrect  .  Blue-domed cysts are gross features of fibrocystic changes, not a Phyllodes tumor. \u25cf  B. Leaf-like lobulations lined by a cytologically benign epithelium, accompanied by increased stromal cellularity, stromal nuclear atypia, and increased mitotic figures.  -  Correct  . Phyllodes tumors and fibroadenomas  are both fibroepithelial lesions. However, Phyllodes tumors typically occur in older women (mean age 40s) and undergo rapid enlargement. Pathologically, Phyllodes tumors are distinguished by their classic leaf-like (phyllodes) lobulated architecture  , lined  by benign epithelium, but with a highly cellular stromal component  demonstrating stromal  nuclear atypia and increased mitotic figures. They exist on a spectrum from benign to malignant based on stromal features, and do not arise from pre-existing fibroadenomas. 194 \u25cf  C. Highly infiltrative borders with cells arranged in single-file cords, accompanied by a robust desmoplastic response.  -  Incorrect  . This  describes invasive lobular carcinoma (ILC), not a Phyllodes tumor. \u25cf  D. Solitary, single-duct arborizing fibrovascular cores lined by a double layer of epithelial cells.  -  Incorrect  . This describes an intraductal  papilloma, not a Phyllodes tumor. \u25cf  E. Intralobular non-caseating granulomas with giant cells, acute inflammation, and micro-abscesses.  -  Incorrect  . This describes chronic  granulomatous mastitis.",
