    "stem": "A 48-year-old female undergoes a breast biopsy showing lobules that are mildly distended and filled with a uniform population of small, round, cytologically atypical cells. The architecture of the acini is effaced, and E-cadherin expression is lost. What is the diagnosis, what is its clinical implication, and what is the associated lifetime risk of developing invasive disease? 183",
