    "stem": "A 24-year-old G0 female presents with a painful, swollen lump on the lower left side of her vulva that makes it difficult to walk or sit. Physical exam reveals a tense, fluctuant, tender 4 cm mass at the 5 o'clock position of the labia majora. What is the diagnosis, and what is the standard first-line management according to the lecture materials?",
