    "stem": "A 24-year-old female with a history of recurrent, untreated PID presents with chronic, dull bilateral lower abdominal pain and primary infertility. Laparoscopy is performed, revealing extensive pelvic adhesions, dilated and tortuous fallopian tubes (hydrosalpinx), and thin, fibrous \"violin-string\" adhesions extending from the liver capsule to the anterior abdominal wall. What is the clinical syndrome involving the liver capsule adhesions, and what are the three major sequelae of PID?",
