    "stem": "A 19-year-old G0 female presents with lower abdominal pain and dyspareunia. On pelvic examination, she is afebrile, but she has exquisite cervical motion tenderness (CMT) and bilateral adnexal tenderness. Speculum exam shows mucopurulent discharge. Her white blood cell (WBC) count is normal, but her C-reactive protein (CRP) is elevated. NAAT for Gonorrhea and Chlamydia is pending. According to CDC guidelines, how is the diagnosis of PID established in this patient, and is a positive STI test required?",
