    "stem": "A 24-year-old male presents to the STI clinic with a single, painless lesion on his penis that appeared 3 weeks after an unprotected sexual encounter. On physical examination, there is a 1 cm, clean-based, indurated, painless ulcer (chancre) on the coronal sulcus, accompanied by non-tender bilateral inguinal lymphadenopathy. What is the stage of this patient's infection, and what is the typical timeline and host immunological response at this stage?",
