    "stem": "A 29-year-old G0 female presents with a diffuse, symmetric, non-pruritic maculopapular rash involving her entire trunk, extremities, palms, and soles, which appeared 6 weeks after she noticed a painless vulvar ulcer that has since healed. She also reports a low-grade fever, sore throat, generalized lymphadenopathy, and several flat, moist, pale-grey papules in her perineal and perianal regions. 232 What is the diagnosis, what are the names of the perineal lesions, and what other systemic manifestations can occur in this stage?",
