    "stem": "A 32-year-old female is diagnosed with latent syphilis after routine screening returns positive RPR and FTA-ABS results. She is completely asymptomatic, has a normal physical exam, and has no history of neurological symptoms. The clinician is trying to determine if her infection represents \"early latent\" or \"late latent\" (or unknown latency) disease. What is the definition of early versus late latent syphilis, and why is this distinction clinically critical?",
