    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "(notched incisors), mulberry molars, saddle nose deformity, and saber shins (anterior bowing of the tibia). \u25cf  A. \"Rhinitis sicca\"; long-term sequelae include osteosarcoma and ameloblastoma. -  Incorrect  . This is a fabricated clinical picture,  and congenital syphilis is not associated with bone cancers like osteosarcoma. \u25cf  B. \"Snuffles\"; long-term sequelae include Hutchinson teeth (notched incisors), mulberry molars, saddle nose deformity, and saber shins (anterior bowing of the tibia).  -  Correct  . The classic early manifestation  of congenital syphilis is  \"Snuffles\"  , which is a highly infectious, thick, purulent, or bloody nasal discharge laden with active Treponema pallidum spirochetes. If untreated in infancy, the disease causes severe long-term developmental and skeletal sequelae  :  Hutchinson  teeth  (widely spaced, centrally notched upper central incisors),  mulberry  molars  (molars with multiple poorly developed cusps resembling a mulberry),  saddle nose  deformity  (destruction of the nasal septum cartilage), and  saber shins  (anterior  bowing of the tibia due to chronic periostitis). \u25cf  C. \"Coryza\"; long-term sequelae include mandibular hyperplasia and supernumerary teeth.  -  Incorrect  . While \"coryza\" is  a general term for runny nose, 250 \"snuffles\" is the specific name for the congenital syphilitic discharge, and the sequelae listed are incorrect. \u25cf  D. \"Ozena\"; long-term sequelae include cleft palate and bilateral hip dysplasia.  - Incorrect  . \"Ozena\" is a chronic atrophic rhinitis,  and the sequelae are incorrect. \u25cf  E. \"Bartholinitis\"; long-term sequelae include vaginal adenosis and clear cell adenocarcinoma.  -  Incorrect  . Bartholinitis is inflammation  of the female vestibulovaginal glands, entirely unrelated to neonatal rhinitis or congenital syphilis sequelae.",
