    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "- **Diagnosis:** A solid ovarian mass producing estrogen (causing postmenopausal bleeding and endometrial hyperplasia) with a yellow gross appearance and lipid-rich cells is a **Thecoma**.\n- **Tumor Characteristics:** \n  - A thecoma is a benign Sex Cord-Stromal tumor composed of theca cells. \n  - Normal theca cells produce androgens from cholesterol. In a thecoma, these cells are often luteinized and contain massive amounts of intracellular lipid (cholesterol), which makes the tumor grossly **yellow** and stains positive for fat (Oil Red O).\n  - The tumor (often in conjunction with surrounding granulosa cells, forming a Fibrothecoma or Granulosa-Theca cell tumor) effectively acts as a massive source of **Estrogen**. The unopposed estrogen causes the bleeding and hyperplasia.\n- **Why Other Choices Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Fibroma:** Composed of fibroblasts (collagen). It is white, not yellow, has no lipid, and does *not* secrete hormones.\n  - **(C) Brenner tumor:** Solid and yellow, but consists of transitional epithelium (urothelium) and does not secrete estrogen.\n  - **(D) Serous cystadenoma:** A water-filled cyst, not a solid lipid-rich tumor.\n  - **(E) Teratoma:** Contains hair/teeth, not a uniform solid lipid tumor.",
    "pearl": "A **Thecoma** is a benign, solid, **yellow** stromal tumor. It is packed with **lipid** (cholesterol) and secretes **Estrogen**, presenting with postmenopausal bleeding.",
