    "stem": "A 60-year-old woman with a history of a prior hysterectomy presents with a large bulge protruding from her vagina. On examination, the physician notes that the bulge is originating from the very top (apex) of the posterior vaginal wall. When the patient bears down, peristaltic bowel sounds can be heard over the bulging vaginal mass using a stethoscope. Which of the following best describes this specific type of pelvic organ prolapse?",
