    "stem": "A 21-year-old woman presents to the clinic with a 3-day history of dysuria, increased vaginal discharge, and intermenstrual spotting. On speculum examination, the cervix appears severely erythematous and edematous, and a thick, yellow, mucopurulent discharge is seen emanating from the endocervical os. The physician suspects cervicitis caused by either *Chlamydia trachomatis* or *Neisseria gonorrhoeae*. Which of the following is the most sensitive and specific diagnostic test to identify the causative organism?",
