    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "- **Complications of PID:** PID is a devastating disease because the intense purulent inflammation (usually caused by Chlamydia/Gonorrhea) destroys the delicate architecture of the reproductive tract.\n- **The Mechanism:** The infection severely damages the ciliated epithelium lining the inside of the fallopian tubes. As the infection heals, it leaves behind dense, fibrotic scar tissue and adhesions. \n  - This scarring narrows the lumen of the tube and creates blind pouches. \n  - If the woman conceives, the fertilized egg (zygote) gets trapped in this scar tissue and cannot travel down into the uterus. Instead, it implants right there in the tube wall, resulting in a life-threatening **Ectopic Pregnancy**.\n  - (The severe scarring also frequently completely blocks the tubes, leading to a massive increase in the risk of **Infertility**).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Endometrial cancer:** Driven by excess estrogen, not bacterial infection.\n  - **(C) Cervical cancer:** Caused by HPV.\n  - **(D) Ovarian failure:** Usually autoimmune or genetic; PID destroys the tubes, but the ovaries typically retain hormonal function.\n  - **(E) Fibroids:** Benign smooth muscle tumors driven by estrogen, unrelated to infection.",
    "pearl": "The two most devastating, long-term complications of **Pelvic Inflammatory Disease (PID)** are **Infertility** and **Ectopic Pregnancy**, both caused by severe fibrotic scarring of the fallopian tubes.",
