    "stem": "A 28-year-old woman is admitted with severe PID. Despite 48 hours of aggressive intravenous antibiotics (Cefoxitin and Doxycycline), her condition worsens. She has persistent high fevers, a leukocytosis of 22,000/$\\mu$L, and a rigid, board-like abdomen with rebound tenderness. Pelvic ultrasound reveals a complex, 8-cm, multiloculated fluid collection in the left adnexa that was not present on an ultrasound done a year ago. What is the most appropriate next step in the management of this patient?",
