    "stem": "A 25-year-old woman is evaluated in the emergency department for severe pelvic pain. She is diagnosed with PID. Her physician is explaining the pathogenesis of her condition to a medical student. The physician notes that while Gonorrhea and Chlamydia are the primary initiators of PID, the destruction of the fallopian tubes is often exacerbated by the subsequent ascent of the patient's own normal vaginal flora. Which of the following normal vaginal organisms is most frequently implicated as a secondary, opportunistic pathogen in polymicrobial PID?",
