    "stem": "A 22-year-old man presents to the clinic in severe distress. Three days ago, he developed tingling and burning on his penis. Today, he has exquisite pain and difficulty urinating. Physical examination reveals a cluster of multiple small, fluid-filled vesicles on an erythematous base located on the glans penis. Several of the vesicles have ruptured, leaving highly tender, shallow ulcers. He also has bilateral, tender inguinal lymphadenopathy. A scraping of the ulcer base is performed (Tzanck smear). Which of the following is the classic finding on this microscopic smear?",
