    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "- **Side Effect Profile of Aromatase Inhibitors:** This is a major testing point comparing AIs to Tamoxifen.\n  - **Tamoxifen (SERM):** Acts as an *agonist* on the bone (protects against osteoporosis). It increases DVT risk and endometrial cancer risk.\n  - **Aromatase Inhibitors (Letrozole, Anastrozole):** Work by completely obliterating all estrogen production in the body. Because there is absolutely zero estrogen left to protect the bone (by increasing OPG and blocking RANKL), patients on AIs suffer rapid, massive bone loss.\n  - **The Consequence:** The most significant, dose-limiting morbidity of AIs is **severe osteoporosis**, massive **joint pain (arthralgias)**, and a high risk of vertebral/hip fractures. (They have no risk of endometrial cancer or DVTs).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Endometrial cancer & (D) DVT:** These are the risks of **Tamoxifen** (due to its partial agonist effects). AIs have no agonist activity anywhere.\n  - **(B) Heart failure:** Trastuzumab or Doxorubicin.\n  - **(E) Peripheral neuropathy:** Paclitaxel (Taxanes) or Platinum agents.",
    "pearl": "**Aromatase Inhibitors** (Anastrozole) obliterate all estrogen, causing severe **Osteoporosis** and severe **joint pain (arthralgias)**. (**Tamoxifen** protects the bone but causes **DVT** and **endometrial cancer**).",
