    "yield_level": "High",
    "stem": "A 25-year-old woman presents to her gynecologist for her annual exam. She has a new sexual partner and is concerned about sexually transmitted infections. She asks about the Human Papillomavirus (HPV) vaccine, noting she has never received it. The physician explains that the bivalent vaccine protects against the two strains of HPV most responsible for cervical cancer. Which of the following characteristics best describes the genetic structure of these high-risk oncogenic viruses?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Single-stranded, positive-sense RNA virus",
      "B": "Double-stranded, circular DNA virus without an envelope",
      "C": "Double-stranded, linear DNA virus with a lipid envelope",
      "D": "Single-stranded, negative-sense RNA virus",
      "E": "Double-stranded RNA virus with a segmented genome"
    },
    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "- **Virology of HPV:** Human Papillomavirus belongs to the Papillomaviridae family.\n- **Viral Structure:** \n  - It is a **DNA virus**.\n  - Its genome is **double-stranded (dsDNA)** and **circular**.\n  - It is **naked (non-enveloped)**. Because it lacks a fragile lipid envelope, it is highly resilient in the environment and resistant to desiccation, which facilitates its transmission via skin-to-skin (or mucosa-to-mucosa) contact.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) ss(+) RNA:** e.g., Hepatitis C, Rubella, SARS-CoV-2.\n  - **(C) dsDNA, linear, enveloped:** e.g., Herpesviruses (HSV, CMV, EBV).\n  - **(D) ss(-) RNA:** e.g., Influenza, Rabies, Measles.\n  - **(E) dsRNA segmented:** e.g., Rotavirus.",
    "pearl": "**Human Papillomavirus (HPV)** is a **naked, double-stranded, circular DNA virus**.",
