    "stem": "A 30-year-old woman with a history of multiple sexual partners and inconsistent condom use is diagnosed with High-Grade Cervical Intraepithelial Neoplasia (CIN III). Laboratory analysis of the cervical tissue confirms the presence of HPV type 16 DNA integrated directly into the host cell chromosomes. The integration of the viral genome into the host DNA typically disrupts the expression of which specific viral regulatory gene, thereby allowing the unchecked, massive overproduction of the oncogenic E6 and E7 proteins?",
