    "stem": "A 35-year-old woman undergoes routine cervical cancer screening via co-testing. Her Pap smear cytology is completely normal (negative for intraepithelial lesion or malignancy). However, her high-risk HPV DNA test returns positive. Based on the most common natural history of HPV infection, which of the following is the most appropriate next step in management for this patient?",
