    "stem": "A 68-year-old woman presents for a routine wellness exam. She asks if she needs a Pap smear. Review of her records shows she has had normal, negative Pap smears every 3 years since she was 25. She has never had an abnormal Pap smear, has never tested positive for HPV, and has been in a monogamous marriage for 40 years. She has not had a hysterectomy. According to current USPSTF guidelines, what is the most appropriate recommendation regarding cervical cancer screening for this patient?",
