    "stem": "A 3-year-old boy is scheduled for surgery to repair bilateral undescended testes (cryptorchidism). During the laparoscopic exploration of the pelvis, the surgeon is astonished to find a typical uterus, bilateral fallopian tubes, and a upper vaginal vault. The testes are found tightly adherent to the fallopian tubes, which has prevented their normal descent into the scrotum. The child's karyotype is 46,XY, and he has typical male external genitalia. What is the diagnosis, and what is the underlying molecular defect?",
