    "rationale": "in the synthesis of AMH or a defect in the AMH receptor. A. Mayer-Rokitansky-Kuster-Hauser (MRKH) syndrome; due to autosomal dominant agenesis of the paramesonephric ducts.:  Incorrect  . MRKH syndrome  occurs in 46,XX females and features congenital absence of the uterus and vagina, which is the exact opposite of PMDS. B. Persistent Mullerian Duct Syndrome (PMDS); due to a deficiency in the synthesis of AMH or a defect in the AMH receptor.:  Correct  . Persistent  Mullerian Duct Syndrome (PMDS) is an autosomal recessive 46,XY DSD caused by a deficiency in the synthesis of Antimullerian Hormone (AMH) by Sertoli cells or a defect in the AMH receptor. Because Leydig cells produce normal testosterone, the Wolffian ducts develop typically into male internal structures and the external genitalia virilize typically. However, because AMH action is absent, the Mullerian ducts fail to regress and differentiate into a uterus and fallopian tubes, which are typically found during cryptorchidism surgery because the uterus prevents typical testicular descent. C. Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS); due to a mutation in the ligand-binding domain of the androgen receptor.:  Incorrect  . CAIS  presents with typically female external genitalia and a blind-ending vagina, not typical male external genitalia with a uterus. D. Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia (CAH); due to a homozygous mutation in the 21-hydroxylase gene.:  Incorrect  . CAH occurs in 46,XX individuals,  resulting in ambiguous genitalia and ovaries, not a 46,XY male with a uterus and testes. E. Swyer syndrome; due to a deletion of the sex-determining region of the Y chromosome.: Incorrect  . Swyer syndrome presents with typical female  external genitalia and streak gonads, not typical male external genitalia and functioning testes.",
