    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "The Differences (Disorders) of Sexual Development (DSD) Classification System organizes these highly complex congenital conditions into three primary categories based on chromosomal and genetic findings. Which of the following correctly pairs a clinical DSD condition with its proper category under this standardized medical classification system? 55",
    "choices": {
      "A": "All DSD conditions that present with ambiguous external genitalia at birth are grouped exclusively under the Sex Chromosome DSD category.",
      "B": "Persistent Mullerian Duct Syndrome (PMDS) is classified as a Sex Chromosome DSD; Swyer syndrome is classified as 46,XX DSD.",
      "C": "Swyer syndrome and Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS) are classified as 46,XY DSD; Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia (CAH) is classified as 46,XX DSD.",
      "D": "Mayer-Rokitansky-Kuster-Hauser (MRKH) syndrome is classified as a Sex Chromosome DSD; 5-alpha-reductase deficiency is classified as 46,XX DSD.",
      "E": "Turner syndrome (45,X) and Klinefelter syndrome (47,XXY) are classified as 46,XX DSD and 46,XY DSD, respectively."
    },
    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "(CAIS) are classified as 46,XY DSD; Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia (CAH) is classified as 46,XX DSD. A. All DSD conditions that present with ambiguous external genitalia at birth are grouped exclusively under the Sex Chromosome DSD category.:  Incorrect  . Many conditions under 68 46,XX DSD (such as CAH) and 46,XY DSD (such as PAIS or 5-alpha-reductase deficiency) present with ambiguous genitalia, but they are not grouped under Sex Chromosome DSD unless there is an aneuploidy. B. Persistent Mullerian Duct Syndrome (PMDS) is classified as a Sex Chromosome DSD; Swyer syndrome is classified as 46,XX DSD.:  Incorrect  .  PMDS and Swyer syndrome are classified as 46,XY DSD, not Sex Chromosome or 46,XX DSD. C. Swyer syndrome and Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS) are classified as 46,XY DSD; Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia (CAH) is classified as 46,XX DSD.:  Correct  . Under the standardized DSD classification system: Group 1 (46,XY DSD) includes conditions such as Swyer syndrome, Complete/Partial Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS/PAIS), 5-alpha-reductase deficiency, and PMDS. Group 2 (46,XX DSD) includes conditions such as Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia (CAH). Group 3 (Sex Chromosome DSD) includes sex chromosome aneuploidies such as Turner syndrome (45,X) and Klinefelter syndrome (47,XXY). D. Mayer-Rokitansky-Kuster-Hauser (MRKH) syndrome is classified as a Sex Chromosome DSD; 5-alpha-reductase deficiency is classified as 46,XX DSD.:  Incorrect  . MRKH is classified as 46,XX DSD, and 5-alpha-reductase deficiency is classified as 46,XY DSD. E. Turner syndrome (45,X) and Klinefelter syndrome (47,XXY) are classified as 46,XX DSD and 46,XY DSD, respectively.:  Incorrect  . Turner syndrome  (45,X) and Klinefelter syndrome (47,XXY) are classified under the Sex Chromosome DSD category, not as 46,XX or 46,XY DSD.",
