    "file": "Notebook_W4_5_Atypical_Development_of_the_20Q.md",
    "qnum": 56,
    "topic": "Atypical Development of the (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A medical student is sketching a summary sheet of the embryological homologies between male and female external genitalia, which develop from the same bipotential precursors under different hormonal influences around the 8th week of development. Which of the following correctly pairs the bipotential embryological precursor with its typical adult male and female derivatives, respectively?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Genital tubercle -> Penile urethra / Labia minora; Urethral folds -> Scrotum / Labia majora; Labioscrotal swellings -> Glans of penis / Clitoris.",
      "B": "Genital tubercle -> Clitoris / Glans of penis; Urethral folds -> Labia majora / Scrotum; Labioscrotal swellings -> Labia minora / Penile urethra.",
      "C": "Genital tubercle -> Shaft of penis / Shaft of clitoris; Urethral folds -> Prostate / Glands of Bartholin; Labioscrotal swellings -> Testes / Ovaries.",
      "D": "Genital tubercle -> Glans of penis / Clitoris; Urethral folds -> Penile urethra / Labia minora; Labioscrotal swellings -> Scrotum / Labia majora.",
      "E": "Genital tubercle -> Scrotum / Labia majora; Urethral folds -> Glans of penis / Clitoris; Labioscrotal swellings -> Penile urethra / Labia minora."
    },
    "correct": "D",
    "rationale": "Penile urethra / Labia minora; Labioscrotal swellings -> Scrotum / Labia majora. A. Genital tubercle -> Penile urethra / Labia minora; Urethral folds -> Scrotum / Labia majora; Labioscrotal swellings -> Glans of penis / Clitoris.:  Incorrect  . This option incorrectly pairs the genital tubercle with the penile urethra (which comes from urethral folds) and labioscrotal swellings with the glans. B. Genital tubercle -> Clitoris / Glans of penis; Urethral folds -> Labia majora / Scrotum; Labioscrotal swellings -> Labia minora / Penile urethra.:  Incorrect  . This option incorrectly pairs the urethral folds with the labia majora (which come from labioscrotal swellings) and labioscrotal swellings with labia minora. 73 C. Genital tubercle -> Shaft of penis / Shaft of clitoris; Urethral folds -> Prostate / Glands of Bartholin; Labioscrotal swellings -> Testes / Ovaries.:  Incorrect  . The penile shaft and clitoral shaft are derived from the genital tubercle, but the prostate and Bartholin's glands are internal outgrowths of the urogenital sinus, and testes/ovaries are gonads. D. Genital tubercle -> Glans of penis / Clitoris; Urethral folds -> Penile urethra / Labia minora; Labioscrotal swellings -> Scrotum / Labia majora.:  Correct  . The bipotential external genitalia precursors develop as follows: 1) The genital tubercle differentiates into the glans penis in males and the clitoris in females; 2) The urethral (urogenital) folds fuse to form the penile urethra in males and remain unfused as the labia minora in females; and 3) The labioscrotal swellings fuse in the midline to form the scrotum in males and remain unfused as the labia majora in females. E. Genital tubercle -> Scrotum / Labia majora; Urethral folds -> Glans of penis / Clitoris; Labioscrotal swellings -> Penile urethra / Labia minora.:  Incorrect  . This option incorrectly pairs the genital tubercle with the scrotum (which comes from labioscrotal swellings) and urethral folds with the glans.",
    "pearl": "",
    "learning_objectives": []
