    "stem": "A 22-year-old G0 female is evaluated for suspected Polycystic Ovary Syndrome (PCOS) due to severe hirsutism, cystic acne, and irregular menses. The physician explains that PCOS is a diagnosis of exclusion and that other pathological causes of excess androgens must be systematically ruled out before confirming the diagnosis. Which of the following lists the primary alternative diagnoses that must be ruled out, and what key screening laboratory tests should be ordered?",
