    "topic": "Menstruation Irregularities (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 32-year-old G0 female presents to her gynecologist with a 6-month history of secondary amenorrhea. Her physical examination is typical, and her BMI is 22.5 kg/m\u00b2. Laboratory evaluation reveals a serum FSH level of 42 mIU/mL on two separate occasions drawn 4 weeks apart, and a serum LH of 28 mIU/mL. Her serum estradiol is undetectable. A pregnancy test is negative. What category of endocrine dysfunction does this patient represent, and what is her diagnosis?",
