    "rationale": "(POI) \u25cf  A. Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism; Kallmann syndrome  -  Incorrect  . Kallmann syndrome features low FSH and LH, not elevated. \u25cf  B. Hypogonadotropic hypogonadism; Functional Hypothalamic Amenorrhea  - Incorrect  . FHA is characterized by low FSH and LH. \u25cf  C. Hypergonadotropic hypogonadism; Primary Ovarian Insufficiency (POI)  - Correct  . This patient presents with  Primary Ovarian  Insufficiency (POI)  (previously termed premature ovarian failure). It is defined as hypergonadotropic hypogonadism occurring before age 40, characterized by  elevated  gonadotropins (specifically FSH > 40 mIU/mL on two separate occasions)  and hypoactive/inactive  ovaries leading to undetectable estradiol and secondary amenorrhea. \u25cf  D. Normogonadotropic hypogonadism; Polycystic Ovary Syndrome  -  Incorrect  . PCOS typically features normal FSH and normal-to-elevated LH, and estradiol is not undetectable. \u25cf  E. Hypergonadotropic hypogonadism; Swyer syndrome  -  Incorrect  . Swyer syndrome presents with primary (not secondary) amenorrhea and streak gonads in a 46,XY individual who has no breast development.",
