    "stem": "An 11-year-old girl is evaluated for delayed puberty. She has a history of severe asthma requiring frequent systemic corticosteroid courses and chronic renal insufficiency. On physical examination, her height is below the 3rd percentile. She has no breast development (Tanner Stage I) and no pubic hair. Her bone age is 8 years. Serum FSH and LH levels are low, and estradiol is undetectable. What category of delayed puberty does this patient represent, and what is the underlying mechanism?",
