    "stem": "A 7-year-old boy is brought to his pediatrician because of rapid growth and early pubertal development. On physical examination, he is tall for his age. His penis is enlarged, scrotal skin is thinned and dark, and there is coarse pubic hair at the base of his penis. However, both of his testes are small and measure 2 mL bilaterally (prepubertal). Basal LH and FSH are low, and serum testosterone is markedly elevated. A brain MRI is normal. What is the most likely diagnosis?",
