    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "alpha-subunit of the Gs protein B. This patient presents with the classic triad of  McCune-Albright syndrome  : 1) peripheral precocious puberty (Tanner Stage III breasts, ovarian cysts, GnRH-independent suppressed LH), 2) caf\u00e9-au-lait spots with jagged 'coast of Maine' borders, and 3) fibrous dysplasia of bone (preposing to recurrent fractures). McCune-Albright syndrome is caused by a sporadic, somatic activating mutation in the Gnas gene  , which encodes  the  alpha-subunit of the Gs protein (G\u03b1s)  . This mutation leads to constitutive activation  of adenylyl cyclase and continuous overproduction of intracellular cAMP, mimicking continuous hormone stimulation in the ovaries, melanocytes, and osteoblasts. A. Loss-of-function mutation in the KAL1 gene, disrupting GnRH neuronal migration:  Incorrect  . Loss-of-function mutations in the KAL1 gene cause Kallmann syndrome, which presents with delayed puberty (hypogonadotropic hypogonadism) and anosmia, not precocious puberty. C. Autosomal recessive mutation in the CYP21A2 gene, causing 21-hydroxylase deficiency: Incorrect  . Mutations in CYP21A2 cause Congenital Adrenal  Hyperplasia (CAH). While CAH can cause precocious pubarche and virilization, it does not cause caf\u00e9-au-lait spots, fibrous dysplasia, or recurrent estrogen-secreting ovarian cysts in this classic triad pattern. D. Deletion of the SRY gene on the Y chromosome:  Incorrect  .  SRY mutations or deletions cause Swyer syndrome, which presents in XY individuals as delayed puberty (streak gonads), not precocious puberty in a 6-year-old XX female. E. Homozygous inactivating mutation in the FSH receptor gene:  Incorrect  . Inactivating FSH receptor mutations cause ovarian resistance, leading to delayed puberty and hypergonadotropic hypogonadism, which is the exact opposite of precocious puberty.",
    "pearl": "",
    "learning_objectives": []
