    "stem": "A 16-year-old female presents with delayed puberty. She has never had a menstrual period. On physical examination, her height is at the 50th percentile, and her body mass index is 21 kg/m2. She has normal Breast Stage I development and absent pubic hair. She complains that she cannot smell perfume or food. Laboratory evaluation shows an FSH of 1.2 mIU/mL and an LH of 0.8 mIU/mL (both low). What is the most likely diagnosis, and what is the underlying embryological pathophysiology?",
