    "stem": "A 13-year-old girl is brought to the clinic for delayed puberty. She has had no breast development and no height acceleration. Her height is below the 3rd percentile. Physical examination is notable for a broad chest with widely spaced nipples, a low posterior hairline, and bilateral 1+ pitting edema of her feet. Laboratory evaluation shows severely elevated serum FSH and LH levels, and undetectable estradiol. What is her most likely karyotype, and what is the underlying gonadal histology?",
