    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 14-year-old girl is evaluated for primary amenorrhea. On physical examination, she has typical breast development (Tanner Breast Stage III) but a complete absence of pubic and axillary hair. Her external genitalia are typically female. Pelvic ultrasound reveals a blind-ending vaginal pouch with no uterus, cervix, or fallopian tubes. Bilateral inguinal masses are palpable, and biopsy confirms they are normal testes. Karyotype is 46,XY. What is the diagnosis, and why does this patient have a complete absence of pubic and axillary hair?",
