    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "complete loss-of-function mutation in the androgen receptor gene, rendering hair follicles unresponsive to circulating androgens 96 B. This patient has Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS), an X-linked recessive 46,XY DSD. Because she has functioning testes, she secretes normal male levels of testosterone and AMH. AMH regresses the Mullerian ducts (no uterus, fallopian tubes, or upper vagina). However, a complete loss-of-function mutation in the androgen receptor (AR) gene makes all target tissues completely blind to testosterone and DHT. Because pubic and axillary hair growth is dependent on androgen action (testosterone/DHT acting on AR), these patients have a complete absence of pubic and axillary hair. A. Mayer-Rokitansky-Kuster-Hauser (MRKH) syndrome; due to complete estrogen receptor insensitivity:  Incorrect  . MRKH syndrome occurs in  46,XX females with normal ovaries and normal, typical pubic/axillary hair (Tanner Stage V), not 46,XY males with testes and absent hair. C. Swyer syndrome; due to an SRY gene deletion preventing the adrenal glands from producing DHEAS:  Incorrect  . Swyer syndrome is characterized  by streak gonads, typical female external genitalia, and sparse pubic hair driven by adrenal androgens, not completely absent pubic hair with normal testes. D. 5-alpha-reductase deficiency; due to an inability of hair follicles to convert testosterone to the more potent androgen DHT:  Incorrect  . In 5-alpha-reductase  deficiency, testosterone levels are normal and androgen receptors are functioning typically. While they have ambiguous external genitalia, they do develop male-pattern pubic and axillary hair at puberty because testosterone acts normally on AR in those follicles. E. Turner syndrome; due to elevated circulating AMH causing hair follicle regression:  Incorrect  . Turner syndrome is 45,X primary ovarian failure and is not characterized by testes, a blind vagina, or absent pubic hair (they have typical pubic hair driven by adrenal androgens).",
    "pearl": "",
