    "stem": "A 16-year-old phenotypic female is evaluated for primary amenorrhea. Physical examination reveals short stature, a broad chest with widely spaced nipples, and a webbed neck. Laboratory evaluation shows severely elevated FSH and LH. Pelvic 85 ultrasound reveals streak gonads and an infantile uterus. Karyotype confirms 45,X. Which of the following represents a known, high-yield genetic or environmental risk factor that can cause primary ovarian failure in chromosomally competent (46,XX) females, mimicking the endocrine findings of this Turner syndrome patient?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Hypothalamic craniopharyngioma",
      "B": "Exogenous testosterone abuse",
      "C": "Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS)",
      "D": "Fragile X Premutation (FMR1 premutation)",
      "E": "McCune-Albright syndrome"
    },
    "correct": "D",
    "rationale": "D. Chromosomally competent (46,XX) females can experience primary ovarian insufficiency (POI), mimicking the hypergonadotropic hypogonadism of Turner syndrome. A classic, high-yield genetic cause of POI in 46,XX females is the Fragile X Premutation (characterized by 60 to 199 CGG repeats in the FMR1 gene). Other causes of POI in competent females include exposure to alkylating chemotherapies, pelvic radiation, galactosemia, and autoimmune oophoritis. A. Hypothalamic craniopharyngioma:  Incorrect  . A craniopharyngioma  is a CNS tumor that suppresses the hypothalamus and pituitary, causing hypogonadotropic hypogonadism (low FSH/LH), not primary ovarian failure (high FSH/LH). B. Exogenous testosterone abuse:  Incorrect  . Exogenous  testosterone suppresses gonadotropins (FSH/LH) via negative feedback, causing secondary hypogonadism, not primary ovarian insufficiency with high FSH/LH. C. Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS):  Incorrect  . CAIS occurs in 46,XY individuals and does not cause premature ovarian failure in 46,XX females. E. McCune-Albright syndrome:  Incorrect  . McCune-Albright  syndrome causes peripheral precocious puberty (GnRH-independent) due to autonomous ovarian cyst estrogen production, not delayed puberty or primary ovarian failure.",
    "pearl": "",
