      "B": "Approximately 90% of reproductive-age women will develop persistent, life-long infections that remain detectable below the standard clinical threshold.",
      "C": "In contrast to women, HPV infection in men is highly persistent, with over 50% of infected men remaining positive at 1 year.",
      "D": "Young women clear HPV infections more rapidly than older women, with more than 70% clearing the infection within 1 year and approximately 90% clearing it within 2 years.",
      "E": "True clearance of HPV never occurs; instead, the virus routinely establishes permanent latent infection in the deep stromal layers of the cervix."
