    "rationale": "the p53 tumor suppressor, preventing apoptosis; E7 binds to and inactivates the retinoblastoma (Rb) protein, releasing the E2F transcription factor to allow unrestricted cell cycle progression. \u25cf  A. E6 binds to and activates the p53 tumor suppressor to trigger cellular senescence, while E7 directly mutates the host DNA mismatch repair genes.  - Incorrect  . E6  inhibits  and degrades p53 (not activates  it), and E7 inactivates Rb, rather than mutating mismatch repair genes. \u25cf  B. E6 inhibits the host cell's retinoblastoma (Rb) protein to block E2F-mediated transcription, while E7 prevents the activation of cyclin-dependent kinases.  - Incorrect  . This swaps the targets (E6 targets p53,  E7 targets Rb) and states that E2F is blocked (Rb inactivation  releases  E2F to promote cell  division). \u25cf  C. E6 binds to and stimulates the ubiquitin-mediated degradation of the p53 tumor suppressor, preventing apoptosis; E7 binds to and inactivates the retinoblastoma (Rb) protein, releasing the E2F transcription factor to allow unrestricted cell cycle progression.  -  Correct  . The cooperative action of  high-risk HPV oncogenes is a classic, high-yield mechanism:  E6 inhibits and degrades p53  (by targeting it for ubiquitin-mediated proteasomal degradation), which prevents p53-dependent apoptosis and cell cycle arrest. Simultaneously,  E7 inactivates  the retinoblastoma (Rb) protein by binding to it, which  releases the E2F transcription  factor  from Rb-mediated inhibition, allowing the cell to bypass the G1/S restriction point and undergo unrestricted cell division. \u25cf  D. Both E6 and E7 act as direct mutagenic alkylating agents that selectively target the promoter region of the PTEN tumor suppressor gene.  -  Incorrect  . E6 and E7 are viral proteins that bind to and dysregulate specific host cell cycle regulatory proteins; they do not act as chemical alkylating agents. \u25cf  E. E6 blocks the transcription of the host L1 and L2 capsid proteins, while E7 prevents the typical post-translational modification of estrogen receptors.  - Incorrect  . These are fabricated mechanisms. 163",
