    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 35-year-old G2P2 female presents for her routine wellness exam and asks about cervical cancer screening. Her 52-year-old mother, who underwent a total abdominal hysterectomy (with removal of the cervix) 5 years ago for benign uterine leiomyomas and has no history of cervical dysplasia, accompanies her and asks if she also needs a Pap smear. According to the USPSTF and ASCCP screening guidelines, which of the following correctly pairs the screening recommendations for both patients?",
