    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "parametrium, vagina, bladder, rectum, urethra, and a portion of the levator muscles. \u25cf  B. The isolated removal of the cervix and paracervical lymph nodes, preserving the uterine corpus and pelvic organs.  -  Incorrect  .  This describes a radical trachelectomy, not pelvic exenteration. \u25cf  C. The laparoscopic ablation of peritoneal endometriosis lesions, combined with a unilateral oophorectomy.  -  Incorrect  . This is a conservative  procedure for benign endometriosis, not a radical cancer salvage operation. \u25cf  D. The resection of the vulva, perineum, and inguinal lymph nodes, sparing the internal pelvic organs.  -  Incorrect  . This describes  a radical vulvectomy, not pelvic exenteration. \u25cf  E. The surgical removal of the pituitary gland and bilateral adrenal glands to eliminate hormone secretion.  -  Incorrect  . This describes  hypophysectomy and adrenalectomy, completely unrelated to pelvic exenteration. \u25cf  A. The surgical resection of the uterus, fallopian tubes, ovaries, parametrium, vagina, bladder, rectum, urethra, and a portion of the levator muscles.  -  Correct  . A total pelvic exenteration  is an ultra-radical salvage  surgical procedure performed for recurrent pelvic cancers (such as cervical cancer) that have failed radiation. It involves the  complete resection of the uterus, fallopian tubes,  ovaries, parametrium, vagina, urinary bladder, urethra, rectum, anus, and a portion of the surrounding levator ani muscles  , requiring the creation of urinary  and fecal diversions.",
