    "stem": "A 45-year-old perimenopausal woman undergoes an oophorectomy for a benign ovarian mass. In the normal, unaffected ovarian cortex, the pathologist observes numerous dense, white, avascular, hyalinized scars composed primarily of type I collagen. There are no recognizable cells or steroidogenic activity within these specific structures. These scars are the physiologic end-stage remnants of which of the following processes?",
