    "stem": "A surgeon is performing a tubal ligation on a 38-year-old woman. She isolates the fallopian tube and plans to excise a small portion of it. To ensure she is cutting the fallopian tube and not the adjacent round ligament of the uterus, she examines the gross and histologic structure. Histologically, the muscularis layer (myosalpinx) of the fallopian tube is arranged in which of the following patterns?",
