    "stem": "A 28-year-old lactating female is breastfeeding her 1-month-old infant. Her breast milk is a highly complex secretion rich in proteins (such as caseins and lactalbumin), lipids (triglycerides), and maternal antibodies. Histological examination of a lactating mammary gland reveals large, dilated alveoli (acini) lined by cuboidal secretory cells, with scarce connective tissue. The pathologist notes that the protein and lipid components of the milk are released from these cells via two entirely different physiological secretory mechanisms. Which of the following correctly pairs the secretory mechanisms of breast milk proteins and lipids, and what is the primary antibody class secreted alongside them?",
