    "file": "Lecture_3_2_Menstrual_Irregularities_HPO_Axis_Set2_30Q.md",
    "qnum": 21,
    "topic": "Lecture 3.2: Menstrual Irregularities and the HPO Axis - Set 2",
    "yield_level": "Mid",
    "stem": "A 55-year-old postmenopausal woman complains of severe vaginal dryness, burning, and painful intercourse (dyspareunia). Physical examination reveals a pale, thin, dry vaginal mucosa with loss of rugae, and the vaginal pH is 6.5. These symptoms and findings are a direct result of the lack of which of the following hormone's trophic effects on the vaginal epithelium?",
