    "rationale": "- **Pathophysiology of Reversal:** Endometrial hyperplasia is caused by unopposed estrogen driving relentless glandular proliferation.\n- **Medical Treatment:** To reverse this, you must overpower the estrogen with a massive dose of its physiologic antagonist: **Progesterone**.\n- **Mechanism of Progestins:** High-dose, continuous progestins (given orally as megestrol acetate, or locally via a Levonorgestrel IUD) exert a powerful anti-estrogenic effect on the endometrium. They halt proliferation, downregulate estrogen receptors, activate enzymes that convert potent estradiol to weak estrone, and induce profound thinning, decidualization, and atrophy of the hyperplastic glands. This can successfully reverse atypical hyperplasia in women wishing to preserve their uterus.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Estrogen:** This is the fuel for the disease; it would rapidly cause progression to cancer.\n  - **(C) Tamoxifen:** An agonist in the uterus; it *causes* hyperplasia.\n  - **(D) Clomiphene:** Induces ovulation; not the primary treatment to reverse active hyperplasia.\n  - **(E) Methotrexate:** Chemotherapy for choriocarcinoma/ectopic pregnancy, not hyperplasia.",
