    "stem": "A 65-year-old male is evaluated for lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS). An MRI of his pelvis is performed. The radiologist notes prominent benign nodules in the transition zone, and a suspicious lesion in the peripheral zone. The central zone appears completely unremarkable. Which of the following correctly describes the glandular percentage of the central zone, the structure it surrounds, and its biological resistance to pathological processes?",
