    "stem": "A 68-year-old male presents with moderate lower urinary tract symptoms (LUTS), including urinary hesitancy, slow stream, and nocturia. On digital rectal exam, his prostate is estimated to be 80 grams. The patient is convinced that his large prostate size is the sole cause of his severe symptoms. Which of the following represents the correct clinical consensus regarding the relationship between prostate size and LUTS, and what are other non-prostatic causes of male LUTS?",
