    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A 27-year-old female presents to her primary care physician due to fatigue, mild weight gain, and oligomenorrhea. Laboratory evaluation demonstrates an elevated TSH of 18.5 mIU/L (typical 0.4\u20134.0) and a low free T4 level, establishing a diagnosis of primary hypothyroidism. The physician explains that her thyroid disorder is the direct cause of her menstrual irregularity. Which of the following describes the correct neuroendocrine mechanism linking primary hypothyroidism to HPO axis disruption? 111",
