    "stem": "A 53-year-old female undergoes an endometrial biopsy due to postmenopausal vaginal bleeding. Her endometrial stripe on ultrasound was measured at 9 mm. The pathologic diagnosis is atypical endometrial hyperplasia (EIN). The gynecologist meets with the patient to discuss treatment options and the risks of declining surgery. According to the lecture materials, what are the progression risks associated with untreated atypical hyperplasia, and what is the standard recommended treatment?",
