      "B": "The risk of progression to cancer is 5% to 10%; combined oral contraceptive pills are the highly recommended first-line treatment.",
      "C": "The risk of progression to cancer is 1% to 3%; expectant management with a repeat biopsy in 3 months is highly recommended.",
      "D": "The risk of progression to cancer is 100% within 1 year; immediate pelvic radiation and chemotherapy are the only recommended treatments.",
      "E": "The risk of progression to cancer is negligible because atypical hyperplasia spontaneously regresses in over 95% of cases without intervention."
