    "qnum": 112,
    "topic": "Uterus Pathophysiology and (Notebook)",
    "yield_level": "Low",
    "stem": "A clinical pathologist receives a biopsy specimen of a peritoneal lesion from a 28-year-old female suspected of having endometriosis. She is performing a microscopic examination to confirm the diagnosis. According to the lecture materials, what are the three classic histologic components that should be present to pathologically confirm the diagnosis of endometriosis?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Smooth muscle fibers, thick-walled blood vessels, and focal areas of geographic coagulative necrosis.",
      "B": "Atypical endometrial glands, squamous metaplasia, and intracellular glycogen vacuoles.",
      "C": "Infantile oocytes, fibrous streak stroma, and multinucleated foreign body giant cells.",
      "D": "Decidualized stromal cells, hypersecretory glands, and prominent spiral arterioles.",
      "E": "Endometrial glands, endometrial stroma, and often hemosiderin-laden macrophages."
    },
    "correct": "E",
    "rationale": "hemosiderin-laden macrophages. \u25cf  A. Smooth muscle fibers, thick-walled blood vessels, and focal areas of geographic coagulative necrosis.  - Incorrect. These  are features of leiomyomas and leiomyosarcomas, not endometriosis. \u25cf  B. Atypical endometrial glands, squamous metaplasia, and intracellular glycogen vacuoles.  - Incorrect. These are not the diagnostic  requirements for endometriosis. \u25cf  C. Infantile oocytes, fibrous streak stroma, and multinucleated foreign body giant cells.  - Incorrect. These are fabricated features  and do not represent endometrial tissue. \u25cf  D. Decidualized stromal cells, hypersecretory glands, and prominent spiral arterioles.  - Incorrect. These are features of typical  secretory endometrium during pregnancy, not diagnostic criteria for endometriosis. \u25cf  E. Endometrial glands, endometrial stroma, and often hemosiderin-laden macrophages.  - Correct. To establish a definitive  pathological diagnosis of endometriosis, histologic evaluation must demonstrate the presence of 1) endometrial glands, 2) endometrial stroma, and 3) hemosiderin-laden macrophages (which accumulate due to chronic cyclic bleeding of the ectopic tissue).",
    "pearl": "",
    "learning_objectives": []
