    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "cytotrophoblast (progenitor layer). A. Outer syncytiotrophoblast (secretes hCG) and inner cytotrophoblast (progenitor layer).: Correct  . Each chorionic villus is lined by two fetal  trophoblastic layers: 1) The outer syncytiotrophoblast, which is a multinucleated syncytium (no distinct cell boundaries) in direct contact with maternal blood in the intervillous space. It secretes hCG, progesterone, estrogen, and hPL; and 2) The inner cytotrophoblast, which consists of a single layer of well-defined cuboidal cells that act as mitotic stem cells to replenish the syncytiotrophoblast. B. Outer peg cells (secrete hCG) and inner ciliated cells (progenitor layer).:  Incorrect  . Peg cells and ciliated cells are epithelial components of the fallopian tubes, not trophoblastic layers of the placental chorionic villi. C. Outer granulosa lutein cells (secrete hCG) and inner theca lutein cells (progenitor layer).: Incorrect  . Granulosa lutein and theca lutein cells  comprise the ovarian corpus luteum, not the placental chorionic villi. D. Outer cytotrophoblast (secretes hCG) and inner syncytiotrophoblast (progenitor layer).: Incorrect  . This is reversed. The syncytiotrophoblast  is the outer multinucleated layer in contact with maternal blood and secretes hCG, while the cytotrophoblast is the inner layer. E. Outer decidual cells (secrete hCG) and inner endothelial cells (progenitor layer).:  Incorrect  . Decidual cells are maternal stromal cells, not fetal trophoblasts, and they do not secrete hCG. Endothelial cells line the fetal capillaries within the villus core.",
    "pearl": "",
    "learning_objectives": []
