    "topic": "Lecture 2.2: Reproductive Development and Disorders of Sex Development (DSDs)",
    "yield_level": "High",
    "stem": "During week 6 of embryologic development, the bipotential gonads consist of an outer cortex and an inner medulla. In a 46,XY fetus expressing normal SRY protein, which of the following histological changes occurs first to firmly establish the fate of the indifferent gonad?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Proliferation of the cortex to form ovarian follicles",
      "B": "Condensation of the medulla into distinct testis cords (medullary cords)",
      "C": "Regression of the mesonephric ducts",
      "D": "Degeneration of the paramesonephric ducts",
      "E": "Invagination of the urogenital sinus"
    },
    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "- **Gonadal Differentiation:** \n  - In a genetic male (46,XY), SRY expression causes the somatic support cells of the gonadal ridge to differentiate into Sertoli cells. \n  - These Sertoli cells rapidly organize and enclose the primordial germ cells, causing the **inner medulla** of the bipotential gonad to condense into solid strands called **testis cords (medullary cords)**. The outer cortex subsequently regresses and forms the thick tunica albuginea. The testis cords will eventually hollow out at puberty to become the seminiferous tubules.\n  - In a genetic female (46,XX), the absence of SRY causes the medulla to regress, while the **outer cortex** proliferates to form ovarian follicles.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Proliferation of cortex:** This is the default *female* pathway.\n  - **(C) Regression of mesonephric ducts:** Occurs in females (due to lack of testosterone).\n  - **(D) Degeneration of paramesonephric ducts:** Occurs in males, but this is a secondary event driven by Anti-Mullerian Hormone (AMH) *after* the testes have formed.\n  - **(E) Invagination of urogenital sinus:** Forms the lower vagina in females.",
    "pearl": "In males (46,XY), the **medulla** develops into **testis cords**, while the cortex regresses. In females (46,XX), the **cortex** develops into **ovaries**, while the medulla regresses.",
