    "stem": "A 3-day-old infant is evaluated for ambiguous genitalia. The karyotype is 46,XY. Laboratory testing reveals perfectly normal, age-appropriate serum levels of testosterone, dihydrotestosterone (DHT), and functional androgen receptors. However, pelvic ultrasound and MRI unexpectedly reveal the presence of a fully formed uterus and fallopian tubes alongside bilateral intra-abdominal testes. A defect in which of the following cell types is most likely responsible for this condition?",
