    "rationale": "- **Clinical Presentation:** The patient has **Persistent Mullerian Duct Syndrome (PMDS)**.\n- **Pathophysiology:** PMDS occurs in 46,XY males who have normal masculinization (normal testosterone/DHT from Leydig cells creating normal male external genitalia and Wolffian ducts). However, they have a defect in either the synthesis of **Anti-Mullerian Hormone (AMH)** by the **Sertoli cells** or a defect in the AMH receptor on the Mullerian ducts.\n- **Outcome:** Because AMH signaling fails, the paramesonephric (Mullerian) ducts do not undergo apoptosis. They persist and develop into a uterus and fallopian tubes, which remain trapped in the abdomen alongside the testes, often preventing normal testicular descent (cryptorchidism).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Leydig cells:** Normal in this patient, evidenced by normal testosterone levels and male external genitalia.\n  - **(C), (D), (E):** Female-specific ovarian cells; absent in a 46,XY individual with SRY.",
