    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "- **Male Internal Genitalia:** The mesonephric (Wolffian) ducts require androgen stimulation to survive and differentiate into the **SEED** structures (Seminal vesicles, Epididymis, Ejaculatory duct, Ductus deferens).\n- **Testosterone Dependence:** Importantly, these ducts lack the enzyme 5$\\alpha$-reductase early in development. Therefore, their differentiation relies entirely on the direct binding of **Testosterone** (secreted by the fetal Leydig cells) to their androgen receptors. \n- **Contrast with External Genitalia:** The genital tubercle and urogenital sinus possess high levels of 5$\\alpha$-reductase and require the much more potent androgen **Dihydrotestosterone (DHT)** to masculinize into the penis, scrotum, and prostate.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) DHT:** Required for *external* genitalia and the prostate, not the internal Wolffian ducts.\n  - **(B) AMH:** Destroys the Mullerian ducts; does not support the Wolffian ducts.\n  - **(D) Estrogen & (E) FSH:** Do not mediate male ductal development.",
    "pearl": "**Testosterone** mediates development of **Internal** male genitalia (Wolffian ducts).\n**DHT** mediates development of **External** male genitalia and Prostate.",
