    "stem": "A 46,XY infant is born in a rural clinic. Examination reveals severe perineoscrotal hypospadias, a bifid scrotum, and a microphallus resembling a clitoris. The testes are palpable in the inguinal canals. Laboratory testing reveals normal levels of testosterone and normal AMH. A defect in the conversion of testosterone to a more potent androgen is suspected. The enzyme responsible for this conversion normally acts primarily on which of the following embryologic structures?",
