    "stem": "A genetic male (46,XY) infant is born with complete androgen insensitivity syndrome (CAIS). The infant has female external genitalia including a clitoris, labia majora, and labia minora. In this patient, the cells that normally give rise to the glans penis have instead differentiated into the clitoris. These cells originate from which of the following embryologic precursor structures?",
