    "rationale": "- **Classic Congenital Adrenal Hyperplasia (CAH):** Due to 21-hydroxylase deficiency, the adrenal cortex shunts precursors into the androgen pathway, bathing the female (46,XX) fetus in high levels of testosterone/androstenedione.\n- **External vs. Internal:** The *external* genitalia virilize because they are sensitive to systemic androgens. However, the *internal* genitalia rely entirely on gonadal programming. The 46,XX fetus has normal ovaries (no SRY). Because there are no testes:\n  - No Sertoli cells $\\rightarrow$ No AMH $\\rightarrow$ **Mullerian ducts survive** (normal uterus/fallopian tubes).\n  - No Leydig cells $\\rightarrow$ No massive *local paracrine* testosterone $\\rightarrow$ **Wolffian ducts degenerate** (systemic adrenal androgens are not high enough locally to save them).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A), (E):** Wolffian structures do not develop.\n  - **(C):** Ovaries are structurally normal, not streaks (as in Turner).\n  - **(D):** Uterus is normal and present.",
    "pearl": "Females (46,XX) with **CAH** have **normal ovaries, normal uterus, and normal tubes**. Only the *external* genitalia are virilized.",
