    "stem": "A 20-year-old woman is evaluated for infertility. She has never had a menstrual period. Physical examination reveals normal breast development, sparse pubic and axillary hair, and a shallow vaginal pouch. Pelvic ultrasound reveals no uterus. Her testosterone level is in the normal male range. The physician diagnoses Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS). What is the recommended management regarding the gonads in this patient?",
