    "stem": "A female neonate is born with ambiguous genitalia, presenting with clitoromegaly and fusion of the labioscrotal folds. During the pregnancy, her mother experienced severe, progressive facial hair growth, deepening of the voice, and clitoromegaly, which entirely resolved after delivery. The infant has normal internal female anatomy (uterus and ovaries). Blood tests on the infant reveal highly elevated testosterone and androstenedione levels, but extremely low estrogen levels. What is the most likely enzyme deficiency in this patient?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "21-hydroxylase",
      "B": "11$\\beta$-hydroxylase",
      "C": "17$\\alpha$-hydroxylase",
      "D": "Placental aromatase",
      "E": "5$\\alpha$-reductase"
    },
    "correct": "D",
    "rationale": "- **Clinical Presentation:** **Aromatase deficiency**.\n- **Pathophysiology:** Aromatase normally converts androgens (androstenedione/testosterone) into estrogens (estrone/estradiol). The placenta is packed with aromatase to protect the mother and female fetus from fetal adrenal androgens.\n- **Maternal Virilization:** If the fetus lacks aromatase, fetal adrenal androgens cannot be converted to estrogen. These massive levels of androgens spill into the maternal circulation, causing the **mother to virilize during pregnancy** (a classic hallmark of this disease). The female fetus also virilizes (ambiguous genitalia).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) 21-hydroxylase & (B) 11$\\beta$-hydroxylase:** Cause CAH and female fetal virilization, but the placenta's aromatase is intact, so it successfully converts the excess fetal androgens to estrogen, preventing *maternal* virilization.\n  - **(C) 17$\\alpha$-hydroxylase:** Causes *lack* of androgens (XY individuals are phenotypic females).\n  - **(E) 5$\\alpha$-reductase:** Only affects males (XY); females are asymptomatic.",
    "pearl": "**Aromatase deficiency** presents with an ambiguous female infant AND **maternal virilization during pregnancy** (due to fetal androgens crossing the placenta un-aromatized).",
