    "yield_level": "High",
    "stem": "A 15-year-old phenotypic female undergoes surgical removal of bilateral streak gonads after being diagnosed with a sex chromosome disorder. The pathology report notes that the streak gonads contain primarily fibrous stroma without any identifiable ovarian follicles or testicular cords. If this patient has a 45,X/46,XY mosaic karyotype, what is the primary clinical rationale for surgically excising these streak gonads?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "To prevent the development of a gonadoblastoma or dysgerminoma",
      "B": "To eliminate the source of excessive androgen production",
      "C": "To induce spontaneous menstruation",
      "D": "To reverse her short stature",
      "E": "To treat primary amenorrhea"
    },
    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "- **Mosaic Turner/DSD:** A patient with a **45,X/46,XY** karyotype has mixed gonadal dysgenesis. They typically present with a female phenotype and streak gonads (similar to Turner syndrome), but some of their cells contain a Y chromosome.\n- **Malignancy Risk:** Any dysgenetic (streak) gonad that contains **Y chromosome material** (e.g., SRY gene fragments) is at a massive, 15-30% lifetime risk of undergoing malignant transformation into a **gonadoblastoma** or a **dysgerminoma**. \n- **Management:** Therefore, unlike classic 45,X Turner syndrome (where the streak gonads are left alone), if a patient has streak gonads and ANY Y-chromosome material (46,XY Swyer or 45,X/46,XY mosaic), prophylactic bilateral gonadectomy is absolutely mandatory as soon as the diagnosis is made.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B) Androgen production:** Streak gonads do not produce significant hormones.\n  - **(C) & (E) Menstruation/Amenorrhea:** Removing the gonads will not induce menses; the patient requires exogenous estrogen/progesterone hormone replacement therapy (HRT).\n  - **(D) Short stature:** Treated with exogenous Growth Hormone (GH), not gonadectomy.",
    "pearl": "Any patient with female phenotype, streak gonads, and **Y chromosome material** (45,X/46,XY or 46,XY Swyer) must undergo **prophylactic gonadectomy** due to extremely high risk of **gonadoblastoma**.",
