    "stem": "A 28-year-old healthy woman is tracking her basal body temperature (BBT) to optimize the timing of conception. She notices a consistent biphasic pattern: her temperature remains relatively low for the first 14 days of her cycle, sharply dips, and then rises by approximately $0.5^\\circ\\text{C} (1^\\circ\\text{F})$ and remains elevated for the next 14 days. Which of the following hormones is directly responsible for this thermogenic shift in basal body temperature?",
