    "stem": "During a normal 28-day menstrual cycle, the anterior pituitary is subjected to varying feedback signals from the ovary. Around day 12, a mature Graafian follicle secretes extremely high, sustained levels of estradiol. In a physiologic paradox, this sustained high estrogen switches from exerting negative feedback to exerting powerful positive feedback on the anterior pituitary. This positive feedback directly triggers the massive release of which of the following?",
