    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "- **Mechanism of COCPs (Combined Oral Contraceptives):** COCPs work by hijacking the normal negative feedback loops of the HPG axis.\n- **Estrogen Component (Ethinyl Estradiol):** The constant, steady state of synthetic estrogen exerts continuous negative feedback on the anterior pituitary. This specifically **suppresses the release of FSH**. Without the initial rise in FSH, no primordial follicles are recruited to grow, and no dominant follicle develops.\n- **Progestin Component:** The progestin component exerts negative feedback to suppress the **LH surge** (preventing ovulation even if a follicle grew). It also thickens the cervical mucus (blocking sperm) and causes endometrial atrophy (preventing implantation).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Thickens cervical mucus & (D) Atrophic endometrium:** These are the primary contraceptive mechanisms of the **Progestin** component, not the estrogen component.\n  - **(B) Premature luteolysis:** COCPs prevent ovulation entirely, so there is no corpus luteum to destroy.\n  - **(E) Uterine contractions:** Not a mechanism of COCPs.",
    "pearl": "In Combined OCPs: \n**Estrogen** $\\rightarrow$ Suppresses **FSH** $\\rightarrow$ prevents follicle development.\n**Progestin** $\\rightarrow$ Suppresses **LH** (prevents ovulation) AND **thickens cervical mucus**.",
