    "stem": "A 29-year-old woman presents to her gynecologist with a chief complaint of breast tenderness, bloating, irritability, and severe mood swings that occur predictably during the final week before her period and resolve completely within two days of the onset of menses. She is diagnosed with Premenstrual Syndrome (PMS). Which of the following hormonal phases is most directly associated with the onset of her symptoms?",
