    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "- **Clinical Presentation:** The patient has **Mullerian Agenesis (Mayer-Rokitansky-K\u00fcster-Hauser / MRKH syndrome)**. \n- **Diagnosis confirmation:** \n  - Absent uterus = Primary amenorrhea.\n  - Normal breasts = Ovaries are working (making estrogen).\n  - **Normal pubic/axillary hair** = Androgen receptors are working perfectly (rules OUT Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome, where hair would be absent). Karyotype is guaranteed to be 46,XX.\n- **Next Step in Management:** The Mullerian ducts develop in extremely close spatial and temporal proximity to the mesonephric ducts and the ureteric buds. Therefore, errors in Mullerian development are highly associated with **renal/urologic anomalies** (e.g., unilateral renal agenesis, pelvic kidney, horseshoe kidney) in up to 30-50% of patients. A **renal ultrasound** is the mandatory next screening step. (Skeletal anomalies of the spine are also common).\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Karyotype:** Not strictly necessary because the presence of normal pubic hair confirms functional androgen receptors, ruling out CAIS. (Though often done in reality for absolute confirmation, renal US is the *highest yield* immediate next clinical step tested on boards).\n  - **(C) Oophorectomy:** Required for CAIS (due to cancer risk in cryptorchid testes), but MRKH patients have normal, healthy, benign ovaries.\n  - **(D) & (E):** She lacks a uterus, so OCPs or GnRH agonists will not induce bleeding or fix the problem.",
