    "rationale": "- **Clinical Presentation:** **Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS)**.\n- **Pathophysiology of Breast Development:**\n  - The SRY gene creates intra-abdominal testes. The Leydig cells produce massive amounts of **testosterone**. \n  - Because the androgen receptors are mutated, the testosterone cannot act on target tissues. \n  - The excess systemic testosterone (and LH-driven androstenedione) is readily converted by the enzyme **aromatase** in peripheral tissues (especially adipose tissue) into **estrogen** (estradiol and estrone).\n  - This unopposed estrogen acts on normal, functional estrogen receptors in the breast tissue, driving excellent, natural breast development.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Direct secretion:** Testes secrete a tiny amount of estradiol, but the vast majority responsible for breast development is from peripheral aromatization of testosterone.\n  - **(C) Adrenal glands:** They produce DHEA, not massive amounts of direct estrogen.\n  - **(D) Maternal estrogens:** Would not persist until puberty to cause breast development.\n  - **(E) Receptor upregulation:** The estrogen receptors are normal, not upregulated; it is the *ligand* (estrogen via aromatization) that is abundant.",
