    "topic": "Lecture 3.2: Menstrual Irregularities and the HPO Axis - Set 1",
    "yield_level": "Mid",
    "stem": "A 17-year-old female presents with primary amenorrhea. She is 5 feet 10 inches tall (95th percentile) and lacks breast development. She reports a lifelong inability to smell. Laboratory evaluation reveals profoundly low serum levels of FSH, LH, and Estradiol. A pelvic ultrasound reveals a small, prepubertal uterus and bilateral normal, unstimulated ovaries. This patient's amenorrhea is caused by a failure of embryologic migration of neurons originating from which of the following locations?",
