    "rationale": "- **Clinical Association:** The patient has POI. Her family history reveals males with intellectual disability (Fragile X syndrome) and adult-onset tremor/ataxia (Fragile X-associated tremor/ataxia syndrome, FXTAS).\n- **Genetics of Fragile X:** Fragile X is caused by a massive CGG trinucleotide repeat expansion in the **FMR1** gene. \n  - $>200$ repeats = Full mutation (causes Fragile X syndrome in males).\n  - **55-200 repeats = Premutation.**\n- **Pathophysiology in Females:** Women who are carriers of the **FMR1 premutation** (55-200 repeats) have a highly elevated risk (~20%) of developing **Primary Ovarian Insufficiency (POI)** before the age of 40. The toxic accumulation of mutant FMR1 mRNA in the oocytes causes accelerated follicular apoptosis.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B) BRCA1:** Causes hereditary breast and ovarian cancer, not POI.\n  - **(C) MECP2:** Causes Rett syndrome (severe neurodevelopmental regression in girls).\n  - **(D) GNAS:** Causes McCune-Albright syndrome (precocious puberty).\n  - **(E) KAL1:** Causes Kallmann syndrome (hypogonadotropic hypogonadism).",
