    "rationale": "- **Clinical Presentation:** The patient presents with **rapid, severe virilization** (deep voice, clitoromegaly, male-pattern baldness). \n- **Differentiating Virilization vs. Hirsutism:** \n  - **PCOS** causes slowly progressive *hirsutism* (excess facial/body hair) and acne, but it almost NEVER causes frank *virilization* (clitoromegaly, voice changes). \n  - Rapid-onset, severe virilization in a female is highly suspicious for an **androgen-secreting tumor**.\n- **The Tumor:** A solid ovarian mass producing massive amounts of testosterone is a **Sertoli-Leydig cell tumor**. These are rare sex cord-stromal tumors of the ovary that differentiate into male structures (Sertoli/Leydig cells) and autonomously secrete androgens, suppressing the HPG axis (amenorrhea) and rapidly virilizing the patient.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) PCOS:** Causes bilateral multiple small cysts, slow onset, hirsutism (not frank virilization), and testosterone is usually only mildly elevated ($<100$ ng/dL).\n  - **(C) Granulosa cell tumor:** Secretes massive amounts of **estrogen**, causing precocious puberty (in kids) or postmenopausal bleeding (in adults), not virilization.\n  - **(D) Dermoid cyst:** Benign germ cell tumor; generally non-functioning (no hormones).\n  - **(E) Choriocarcinoma:** Secretes massive **hCG**, mimicking pregnancy/hyperthyroidism.",
