    "stem": "An 11-year-old girl is evaluated by her pediatrician. On physical examination, the physician notes elevation of the breast and papilla as a small mound, with enlargement of the areolar diameter. The pubic hair is sparse, lightly pigmented, and straight, located mainly along the medial border of the labia majora. Based on the Tanner staging system, what stage of breast and pubic hair development does this patient currently exhibit?",
    "choices": {
      "A": "Tanner Stage I",
      "B": "Tanner Stage II",
      "C": "Tanner Stage III",
      "D": "Tanner Stage IV",
      "E": "Tanner Stage V"
    },
    "correct": "B",
    "rationale": "- **Tanner Staging (Sexual Maturity Rating):**\n  - **Stage I:** Prepubertal. No breast tissue; no pubic hair.\n  - **Stage II:** **Breast bud** forms (elevation of breast/papilla, areolar enlargement). Pubic hair is **sparse, straight, and lightly pigmented** along the labia majora. (This represents the onset of puberty).\n  - **Stage III:** Breast mound enlarges further without separation of contours. Pubic hair becomes **darker, coarser, and curly**, extending over the mons pubis.\n  - **Stage IV:** Areola and papilla project to form a **secondary mound** above the level of the breast. Pubic hair is adult-like in type but not volume (does not spare the medial thighs).\n  - **Stage V:** Adult breast contour (areola recedes to general contour of the breast). Adult pubic hair quantity, extending to the medial thighs in an inverse triangle.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Stage I:** Complete absence of signs.\n  - **(C) Stage III:** Curly, dark pubic hair; larger breasts.\n  - **(D) Stage IV:** Secondary mound of the areola.\n  - **(E) Stage V:** Fully mature adult.",
    "pearl": "**Tanner Stage II** is the clinical hallmark of the **onset of puberty**: represented by the **breast bud** (thelarche) in girls and **testicular enlargement** (volume $>4$ mL) in boys.",
