    "stem": "A 12-year-old boy is brought to the clinic by his parents who are concerned about his physical development compared to his peers. On examination, the physician calculates his testicular volume to be 5 mL bilaterally using a Prader orchidometer. His penis has not significantly lengthened, and there is no pubic hair. According to normal male pubertal milestones, what does this physical finding signify?",
