    "stem": "A 19-year-old female presents with primary amenorrhea. She has completely normal breast development and female external contours. However, her pubic and axillary hair are completely absent. Pelvic examination reveals a blind-ending vagina. Ultrasound shows an absent uterus and ovaries, but two solid masses are noted in the inguinal canals. Laboratory testing reveals testosterone levels in the upper normal male range. Which of the following is the most likely diagnosis?",
