    "stem": "A 16-year-old boy is evaluated for delayed puberty. He has a history of cleft lip and palate repaired in infancy. He notes that he cannot smell coffee or peppermint. On examination, his testicular volume is 2 mL bilaterally, and he has no pubic hair. Serum testing shows low testosterone, low FSH, and low LH. Which of the following pathophysiologic mechanisms is the fundamental cause of his condition?",
