    "stem": "A 16-year-old girl is evaluated for delayed puberty. She is tall, with long limbs, and lacks secondary sexual characteristics. She complains of fatigue, weight gain, and cold intolerance. Physical examination reveals an enlarged, firm, painless thyroid gland. Her serum FSH and LH are low, and prolactin levels are markedly elevated. Which of the following is the most likely underlying cause of her delayed puberty?",
