    "stem": "A 22-year-old male is undergoing an evaluation for infertility. He has a history of cystic fibrosis (homozygous for the $\\Delta$F508 mutation). Physical examination reveals normal testicular volume, normal virilization, and the absence of any palpable structures in the posterolateral aspect of the testes. A semen analysis reveals profound azoospermia (zero sperm in the ejaculate). His serum FSH, LH, and testosterone levels are completely normal. What is the precise anatomic cause of this patient's infertility?",
