    "correct": "A",
    "rationale": "- **Differentiating Absent Uterus Syndromes:** \n  - Both **M\u00fcllerian Agenesis (MRKH, 46,XX)** and **Complete Androgen Insensitivity Syndrome (CAIS, 46,XY)** present with primary amenorrhea, an absent uterus, and completely normal breast development (via ovarian estrogen in MRKH, and aromatized testicular testosterone in CAIS).\n- **The Key Difference:** \n  - **Pubic/Axillary Hair:** The growth of body hair in phenotypic females is driven by adrenal androgens binding to androgen receptors. \n  - In **MRKH (46,XX)**, the androgen receptors work perfectly. Therefore, they have **normal, abundant pubic and axillary hair**.\n  - In **CAIS (46,XY)**, the androgen receptors are completely defective. Therefore, they have **absent or extremely sparse pubic and axillary hair**.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(B) Breast tissue:** Present and normal in both.\n  - **(C) Vaginal pouch:** Both have a blind-ending shortened vaginal pouch.\n  - **(D) Height:** CAIS patients tend to be slightly taller (due to Y chromosome), but height is not a reliable diagnostic discriminator compared to body hair.\n  - **(E) Acne:** Absent in CAIS, but highly variable in MRKH.",
    "pearl": "Absent uterus + Normal breasts + **Normal pubic hair** = **M\u00fcllerian Agenesis (MRKH, 46,XX)**.\nAbsent uterus + Normal breasts + **Absent pubic hair** = **CAIS (46,XY)**.",
