    "rationale": "- **Endometrial Cancer Protection:** The primary driver of Type I endometrial cancer is unopposed estrogen. To protect the uterus, you must provide **Progesterone**.\n- **Combination Oral Contraceptive Pills (COCPs):** These pills contain both estrogen and a synthetic **progestin**. \n- **The Mechanism:** The progestin component dominates the pill's effect on the uterus. It prevents the estrogen from hyper-stimulating the lining. It causes the endometrium to remain thin and atrophic, and completely prevents hyperplasia. \n- **The Benefit:** Using COCPs for just a few years cuts the lifetime risk of endometrial cancer (and ovarian cancer) by **$50\\%$**, and this protective effect lasts for decades after stopping the pill.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) Copper IUD:** Causes local inflammation to kill sperm; no hormones, no protection against cancer. (A *Levonorgestrel* IUD does protect, but Copper does not).\n  - **(B) Tubal ligation & (C) Condoms & (E) Rhythm method:** Provide mechanical/behavioral contraception; no hormonal effect on the uterus.",
