    "rationale": "- **Molecular Pathology of Type II Endometrial Cancer:**\n  - **Type II (Serous)** carcinoma is a highly aggressive, poorly differentiated, estrogen-independent tumor.\n  - The absolute hallmark molecular lesion (found in $>90\\%$ of cases) is an acquired somatic mutation in the **TP53 tumor suppressor gene**. \n  - Without functional p53 (the \"guardian of the genome\"), the cells accumulate massive DNA damage, leading to severe nuclear pleomorphism and rapid, aggressive malignant growth.\n- **Why Other Choices Are Incorrect:**\n  - **(A) PTEN:** The classic, early mutation in **Type I** (Endometrioid/estrogen-driven) endometrial cancer.\n  - **(C) KRAS:** Associated with Type I endometrial cancer (along with PTEN), colon cancer, and pancreatic cancer.\n  - **(D) BRCA2:** Breast and ovarian cancer.\n  - **(E) APC:** Colon cancer (FAP).",
    "pearl": "**Type I** Endometrial Cancer = **PTEN** mutations.\n**Type II** (Serous) Endometrial Cancer = **TP53** mutations.",
