    "stem": "A 68-year-old woman is diagnosed with Type II (Serous) Endometrial Carcinoma via biopsy. She undergoes a total abdominal hysterectomy, bilateral salpingo-oophorectomy, and extensive pelvic and para-aortic lymph node dissection. The surgeon also meticulously inspects the omentum and peritoneal surfaces, taking multiple biopsies. Why is such an aggressive surgical staging approach required for Type II endometrial cancer compared to Type I?",
