    "yield_level": "Mid",
    "stem": "During a radical prostatectomy for prostate adenocarcinoma, the surgeon is carefully dissecting the posterior capsule of the prostate. To prevent postoperative erectile dysfunction, the surgeon must preserve the cavernous nerves, which travel within the neurovascular bundles. These parasympathetic nerves, responsible for penile erection, arise from which of the following spinal cord segments?",
