    "stem": "A 70-year-old male with locally advanced prostate cancer undergoes a radical retropubic prostatectomy. Three months postoperatively, he presents with profound erectile dysfunction. He reports no issues with urinary continence. The surgeon suspects injury to the autonomic nerve fibers that supply the corpora cavernosa. These injured nerve fibers travel immediately adjacent to which of the following fascial structures during their course to the penis?",
