    "stem": "During a routine vasectomy, a urologist makes a small incision in the anterior scrotum, isolates the ductus (vas) deferens, and ligates it bilaterally. The layers of the spermatic cord and scrotum must be dissected to reach the vas deferens. The innermost fascial layer immediately surrounding the vas deferens is the internal spermatic fascia. This specific fascial layer is embryologically derived from which of the following abdominal wall structures?",
