    "yield_level": "High",
    "stem": "A 60-year-old male undergoes a radical cystoprostatectomy for invasive bladder cancer. Following the removal of the bladder and prostate, the pathologist notes that the fascial layer separating the posterior aspect of the prostate from the anterior wall of the rectum is entirely intact, confirming negative posterior surgical margins. What is the eponym for this crucial tough fascial layer that acts as a barrier preventing direct posterior spread of prostate cancer into the rectum?",
