    "stem": "During an open appendectomy for acute perforated appendicitis in a 24-year-old male, the surgeon makes a McBurney's incision. As the surgeon cuts through the aponeurosis of the external oblique muscle, a small nerve is identified running over the spermatic cord just as it emerges from the superficial inguinal ring. This nerve is at high risk of transection. What area of the body will experience sensory loss if this nerve is severed?",
