    "stem": "A 24-year-old woman presents with intense vulvar itching and a thick, white, \"cottage-cheese-like\" vaginal discharge. She recently completed a course of oral amoxicillin for a sinus infection. On examination, the vulva is erythematous and edematous, but there is no skin thinning or labial fusion. A wet mount of the discharge prepared with KOH reveals branching pseudohyphae. The pathogenesis of this patient's vulvar disorder is most accurately described by which of the following mechanisms?",
