    "stem": "A 42-year-old woman with a 20-pack-year smoking history presents with a raised, fleshy, warty lesion on her right labium majus. A biopsy reveals Vulvar Intraepithelial Neoplasia (VIN) grade III (high-grade squamous intraepithelial lesion). The pathologist notes koilocytic atypia and disordered squamous maturation. This precancerous lesion is most strongly associated with infection by which of the following pathogens?",
