    "stem": "A 22-year-old woman presents to the clinic with multiple painless, cauliflower-like fleshy growths on her perineum and vulva. She is diagnosed with condyloma acuminatum (genital warts). Her physician applies a topical treatment (imiquimod) to clear the lesions. Although these lesions can be large and disfiguring, the physician reassures her that they have an extremely low risk of progressing to invasive cancer. These benign lesions are most commonly caused by which of the following viruses?",
