    "stem": "A pathologist is examining a biopsy of a pigmented vulvar lesion. The differential diagnosis is between Extramammary Paget Disease and superficial spreading Vulvar Melanoma, as both can present with large, atypical cells infiltrating the epidermis. The pathologist orders an immunohistochemical panel. Which of the following staining profiles would definitively confirm the diagnosis of Vulvar Melanoma and rule out Paget Disease?",
