    "rationale": "- **Hypospadias Pathogenesis:** Failure of the paired **urogenital (urethral) folds to completely fuse in the midline along the ventral surface of the penis**, leaving the external urethral meatus abnormally situated on the ventral aspect of the glans, corona, penile shaft, or perineum.\n- **Etiology:** Deficient androgen production (testosterone/DHT) or defective androgen receptor signaling during weeks 8\u201314 of gestation.\n- **Clinical Rule:** **Circumcision is strictly contraindicated!** The dorsal prepuce (foreskin) must be preserved because it is utilized as vascularized skin graft tissue during surgical reconstruction (usually performed at 6\u201312 months of age).\n- **Contrast with Epispadias:** Meatus opens on the **dorsal (upper)** surface of the penis due to faulty positioning of the **genital tubercle**, classically associated with **bladder exstrophy**.",
