    "topic": "Pelvic Anatomy & Perineum",
    "yield_level": "High",
    "stem": "A 16-year-old phenotypic female presents with primary amenorrhea and absent pubic and axillary hair. Karyotype reveals 46,XY. Pelvic imaging shows a blind-ending vagina without a uterus or ovaries, and undescended testes are found in the inguinal canals. Which is the most likely diagnosis?",
