    "correct": "C",
    "rationale": "Complete androgen insensitivity syndrome (AIS) is X-linked recessive; 46,XY individuals have functioning testes that produce testosterone and AMH, but target tissues cannot respond due to androgen receptor defects. This results in normal female external genitalia (short, blind-ending vagina), absent uterus/ovaries (due to functional AMH), undescended testes, and absent pubic/axillary hair (androgen-dependent).",
